window.IAS_GUIDE_DATA = {"chapters":[{"week":9,"title":"Access Control","subtitle":"කවුද, මොන දේට, මොන වැඩේ කරන්න අවසර තියෙන්නේ?","pages":[3,7],"intro":"හැමෝම එකම university portal එකට login වුණත් හැමෝටම එකම බලතල ලැබෙන්නේ නැහැ. Student කෙනෙකුට තමන්ගේ ලකුණු බලන්න පුළුවන්; lecturer කෙනෙකුට තමන්ට භාර පාඨමාලාවේ ලකුණු වෙනස් කරන්න පුළුවන්. මේ වෙනස තීරණය කර ක්‍රියාත්මක කරන්නේ Access Control එකයි.","objectives":["Separate authentication from authorization.","Choose DAC, MAC or RBAC from the decision basis.","Read and construct an access matrix, ACL and capability view.","Apply least privilege, separation of duty and dual control."],"topics":[{"id":"access-foundations","title":"9.1 Identity, resources and allowed actions","pages":[3,4],"si":["දොරටුවේදී ඔබ කවුද කියා තහවුරු කිරීමත්, ඇතුළට ගිය පසු ඔබට මොන වැඩ කරන්න පුළුවන්ද කියා තීරණය කිරීමත් වෙනස් වැඩ දෙකක්. Username එකෙන් identity එක claim කරනවා. Authentication එකෙන් එය පරීක්ෂා කරනවා. Authorization එකෙන් resource එක සහ ඉල්ලන action එකට අවසර තිබේද බලනවා.","Access request එකක් දුටුවාම ප්‍රශ්න තුනක් අහන්න: කවුද ඉල්ලන්නේ? මොන දේටද? මොන වැඩක් කරන්නද? ඒවා පිළිවෙළින් Subject, Object සහ Access Right යන කොටස් තුනයි. Subject එක user කෙනෙකු හෝ user වෙනුවෙන් වැඩ කරන process එකක් විය හැකියි."],"definition":{"term":"Access Control","text":"Policies and mechanisms that prevent unauthorized use of resources, including actions an otherwise authorized user is not permitted to perform."},"diagram":"access-flow","table":{"headers":["Element","Meaning","University example"],"rows":[["Subject","Entity requesting access","Lecturer or a process acting for the lecturer"],["Object","Resource being protected","Examination mark record"],["Access right","Operation requested or permitted","Read, Write/Update, Execute, Delete, Create or Search"],["Authorization","Decision about the requested action","Allow editing only for an assigned course"]]},"example":{"q":"A lecturer uses the university portal to update examination marks. Identify the subject, object and access right.","steps":["Identify the actor requesting the operation: the lecturer.","Identify the resource affected: the examination marks record.","Identify the requested operation: Write/Update."],"answer":"Subject: the lecturer (or the portal process acting for the lecturer). Object: the examination mark record. Access right: Write/Update. The policy must also restrict the update to records the lecturer is authorized to edit.","si":"“Update” කියන වචනය action එක හඳුනාගන්න උදව් වෙනවා. Portal එක මෙහි භාවිත කරන මාර්ගයයි; ආරක්ෂා කළ යුතු object එක ලකුණු record එකයි. Login සාර්ථක වූ බව පමණක් බලලා edit අවසර දෙන්න බැහැ."},"trap":{"en":"Successful authentication does not imply permission to use every resource.","si":"“Login වුණා” සහ “මේ record එක edit කරන්න අවසර තියෙනවා” කියන තීරණ දෙක වෙන් කර ලියන්න."}},{"id":"policy-models","title":"9.2 DAC, MAC and RBAC: identify the decision basis","pages":[4,5],"si":["Policy එක හඳුනාගන්න ක්‍රමය system එකේ නම මතක තබාගැනීම නොවෙයි. අවසර තීරණය කරන පදනම බලන්න. File owner කෙනෙකු තමන්ගේ කැමැත්තෙන් sharing permissions දෙනවා නම් DAC. Security labels සහ user clearance අනුව මධ්‍යගත නීතියක් තීරණය කරනවා නම් MAC.","Job function එක අනුව permissions බෙදාදෙනවා නම් RBAC. Hospital එකක Doctor, Nurse, Receptionist වැනි roles වලට අවශ්‍ය වැඩ වෙනස් නිසා එක් එක් role එකට අවශ්‍ය permissions දී users ඒ roles වලට assign කරනවා. සැබෑ system එකක මේ models කිහිපයක් එකට භාවිත කළ හැකියි."],"definition":{"term":"Access-control policy models","text":"DAC uses authorized-owner discretion; MAC enforces centrally controlled classifications and clearances; RBAC assigns permissions to roles and assigns users to those roles."},"diagram":"policy-models","table":{"headers":["Model","Decision basis","Good-fit example","Limitation"],"rows":[["DAC","Owner/authorized entity grants rights","Owner shares a collaborative file","Owners may grant excessive access"],["MAC","Labels, clearances and mandatory rules","Classified defense records","Label administration and flexibility can be difficult"],["RBAC","Role membership and role permissions","Doctor, nurse and clerk duties","Too many poorly designed roles can create excess privilege"]]},"example":{"q":"Doctors edit clinical notes, nurses view care instructions, and clerks manage appointments. Which model best fits, and why?","steps":["The access differences correspond to job functions.","Define Doctor, Nurse and Clerk roles.","Attach suitable permissions to each role, then assign users to roles."],"answer":"RBAC is the best fit because access is determined by job roles. Doctors receive appropriate clinical-edit rights, nurses receive permitted care-view rights, and clerks receive appointment-management rights. Enforce finer patient/record restrictions where required.","si":"මෙහි owner කෙනෙකු කැමැත්තෙන් file share කරන කතාවක් නැහැ. Job role එක වෙනස් වීමෙන් permission වෙනස් වෙන නිසා RBAC කියා හේතුවත් සමඟ ලියන්න."},"trap":{"en":"MAC in Week 9 means Mandatory Access Control; MAC in cryptography means Message Authentication Code.","si":"MAC කියන කෙටි නම දැක්කාම ප්‍රශ්නය access permissions ගැනද, message authentication ගැනද කියා මුලින් බලන්න."}},{"id":"matrix-acl-capabilities","title":"9.3 Access matrix, ACLs and capabilities","pages":[5,6],"si":["Access Matrix එක වගුවක් ලෙස හිතන්න. පේළිවල Subjects ද, තීරුවල Objects ද දානවා. මැද cell එකක ඒ subject ට ඒ object එක සම්බන්ධයෙන් තිබෙන rights ලියනවා. R පමණක් තිබුණොත් Read පමණයි; W නැත්නම් Write කරන්න අවසර නැහැ.","එකම matrix එක දෙපැත්තකින් කියවන්න පුළුවන්. එක object එකේ තීරුව බැලුවාම “මේ file එකට කාට මොන rights ද?” කියන ACL view එක ලැබෙනවා. එක subject එකේ පේළිය බැලුවාම “මේ holder ට මොන resources වල මොන වැඩ කරන්න පුළුවන්ද?” කියන capability view එක ලැබෙනවා. Capability token එකක් අතේ තිබීමෙන් බලතල ලැබිය හැකි නිසා එය forge කිරීමෙන් සහ සොරකම් කිරීමෙන් ආරක්ෂා කළ යුතුයි."],"definition":{"term":"Access Matrix","text":"A table whose subject rows and object columns contain the access rights permitted for each subject–object pair."},"diagram":"matrix","table":{"headers":["Subject / Object","Grades","Course notes","Accounts"],"rows":[["Student","R: own results only","R","—"],["Lecturer","R,W: assigned courses","R,W","—"],["System administrator","— unless separately approved","— unless separately approved","R,W / account management as granted"]]},"bullets":[{"en":"ACL: object-centred; inspect a matrix column.","si":"එක file එකට access තියෙන සියලු users සහ rights බැලීමට පහසුයි."},{"en":"Capability: holder-centred; inspect the rights available to a holder.","si":"එක holder කෙනෙකුට භාවිත කළ හැකි resources සහ operations බැලීමට පහසුයි."},{"en":"Capabilities must be unforgeable and protected from theft.","si":"අනුන්ට token එක හදාගන්න හෝ සොරකම් කර භාවිත කරන්න හැකි නම් authorization ආරක්ෂාව බිඳෙනවා."}],"example":{"q":"A Student–Grades cell contains R only. Can the student write a new grade?","steps":["Locate the Student row.","Locate the Grades column.","Read the cell: it grants R, not W."],"answer":"Deny the write request. Read permission is granted, but Write permission is absent. Rights must follow the stated policy; do not infer Write from Read or Read from Write.","si":"Cell එකේ දී තිබෙන permission එක පමණක් භාවිත කරන්න. “Student ට file එක පේනවා, ඒ නිසා වෙනස් කරන්නත් පුළුවන්” කියන අනුමානය වැරදියි."},"trap":{"en":"Use subject rows and object columns; do not reverse ACL and capability views.","si":"Rows = Subjects, Columns = Objects, Cells = Rights කියා matrix එකට ලේබල් දාලා පටන් ගන්න."}},{"id":"rbac-requirements","title":"9.4 RBAC and the eight access-control requirements","pages":[6,7],"si":["RBAC එකේ User → Role → Permission මාර්ගය මතක තබාගන්න. User කෙනෙකුට roles කිහිපයක් තිබිය හැකියි; එක role එක users කිහිපදෙනෙකුට දිය හැකියි. ඒක many-to-many සම්බන්ධයක්. අලුත් role එකක් එකතු කරන විට පරණ role එකේ අනවශ්‍ය අවසර ඉවත් නොකළොත් privileges ටිකෙන් ටික වැඩි විය හැකියි.","Least Privilege කියන්නේ වැඩේට අවශ්‍ය අවම permissions පමණක් දීමයි. Separation of Duty කියන්නේ වැදගත් වැඩේ පියවර වෙනස් පුද්ගලයන් අතර බෙදීමයි. Dual Control කියන්නේ එක සංවේදී action එකකට පුද්ගලයන් දෙදෙනෙකු හෝ වැඩි ගණනක් එක්ව අවසර දීමයි. මේ අවසාන දෙක සම්බන්ධ වුණත් එකම අදහස නොවෙයි."],"definition":{"term":"RBAC and secure administration","text":"RBAC associates permissions with roles and users with roles. Secure access administration also needs reliable inputs, suitable granularity, least privilege and clearly defined policy rules."},"diagram":"rbac","table":{"headers":["Requirement","Exam meaning","Example"],"rows":[["Reliable input","Use trustworthy identity and policy attributes","Verify user identity before granting access"],["Fine / coarse granularity","Control a field/record or a broader resource","Own marks versus the whole marks table"],["Least Privilege","Grant only necessary rights","Student reads only permitted results"],["Separation of Duty","Different people perform separate critical steps","One person creates, another approves"],["Open / Closed policies","Default allow / default deny","Deny unless expressly permitted"],["Conflict resolution","Define which conflicting rule wins","Deny-overrides where the policy specifies it"],["Administrative policies","Define who may change permissions","Only an authorized administrator assigns roles"],["Dual Control","Multiple authorized people jointly authorize an action","Two signatories approve a high-value transfer"]]},"example":{"q":"One clerk creates an invoice and another approves it. A high-value transfer separately requires two joint approvals. Name both concepts.","steps":["Creating and approving are separate workflow tasks.","Different people perform these tasks.","The transfer requires joint participation in one sensitive authorization."],"answer":"Invoice creation versus approval illustrates Separation of Duty. Requiring two authorized people to jointly approve the high-value transfer illustrates Dual Control. Both can be used together.","si":"වෙනස් පියවර දෙක වෙනස් අයට දෙන එක SoD. එකම transfer එකට දෙන්නෙකුගේ joint approval අවශ්‍ය කරන එක Dual Control. ප්‍රශ්නයේ ක්‍රියාවට සම්බන්ධ කර වෙනස පැහැදිලි කරන්න."},"trap":{"en":"An administrator role should not automatically receive every business-data permission.","si":"Accounts manage කරන බලය තිබුණා කියලා සියලු රහස් records කියවීමේ බලයත් අනිවාර්යයෙන් ලැබෙන්නේ නැහැ."}}],"checkpoint":[{"q":"Which model best fits a document owner deciding who may read a file?","a":"DAC — Discretionary Access Control.","si":"Ownerගේ sharing තීරණය මෙහි පදනමයි."},{"q":"Which model fits classified military records and user clearances?","a":"MAC — Mandatory Access Control.","si":"Classification සහ clearance අනුව මධ්‍යගත policy එක ක්‍රියා කරයි."},{"q":"Which direction of a matrix gives an object’s ACL?","a":"The object column.","si":"එක object එකේ තීරුවෙන් එයට access තියෙන subjects දැකගන්න පුළුවන්."},{"q":"Which principle limits rights to what the task needs?","a":"Least Privilege.","si":"වැඩේට අවශ්‍ය අවම අවසර පමණක් දෙන්න."},{"q":"Why must a capability ticket be protected?","a":"It represents authority and must resist forgery, theft and misuse.","si":"Token එක අතේ තිබීමෙන් අවසර ලැබිය හැකි නිසා එය අනුන්ට අතට පත්වීම අවදානමක්."}],"summary":"Week 9 අවසානයේ matrix එකක් ඔබම අඳින්න. User, role සහ permission අතර සම්බන්ධය trace කරන්න. Scenario එකක DAC, MAC හෝ RBAC තෝරන විට නමත්, ඒ model එක ගැළපෙන හේතුවත් එකට ලියන්න."},{"week":10,"title":"User Authentication","subtitle":"කියන identity එක ඇත්තද කියා පරීක්ෂා කරමු","pages":[8,14],"intro":"Username එක දැනගැනීමෙන් පමණක් system එකට ඇතුළු වීමට අවසර දිය නොහැකියි. Authentication එකේ වැඩේ ඒ identity එක claim කරන පුද්ගලයාට එයට අදාළ සාක්ෂිය තිබේද පරීක්ෂා කිරීමයි. ඉන්පසුව authorization මගින් resource එකකට මොන වැඩ කළ හැකිද තීරණය කරනවා.","objectives":["Separate identification, verification and authorization.","Classify authentication factors and evaluate MFA combinations.","Recognize all eight password-attack scenarios and suitable controls.","Explain salted verification, SSO and nonce-based replay protection."],"topics":[{"id":"authentication-identity","title":"10.1 Identification, verification and authorization","pages":[8],"si":["Identification කියන්නේ “මම මේ account එකේ user” කියා නම හෝ ID එක ඉදිරිපත් කිරීමයි. Verification කියන්නේ එම claim එකට සාක්ෂිය පරීක්ෂා කිරීමයි. Password, token හෝ biometric evidence එකක් එයට භාවිත කළ හැකියි.","Authentication සාර්ථක වූ පසුත් resource එකට යවන සෑම action එකක්ම authorization policy එකෙන් පරීක්ෂා කළ යුතුයි. Student කෙනෙකුට login වීමට හැකි වුණත් lecturer-only grade editor එකට ඇතුළු වීමට නොහැකි වීම මේ වෙනසට හොඳ උදාහරණයක්."],"definition":{"term":"Authentication","text":"The process of verifying an identity claimed by or for a system entity."},"diagram":"identity","table":{"headers":["Step","Question being answered","Example"],"rows":[["Identification","Who do you claim to be?","Enter Student ID"],["Verification / authentication","Can the claim be substantiated?","Check password or token"],["Authorization","May this identity perform this action?","Allow view-own-marks but deny mark editing"]]},"example":{"q":"A student enters a username and password. Login succeeds, but access to the lecturer-only grade editor is denied. Classify the steps.","steps":["Username identifies the account.","Password verification supports authentication.","The grade-editor decision evaluates permissions."],"answer":"Username entry is Identification; checking the password is Verification within Authentication; denying the lecturer-only operation is Authorization. A successful login does not grant the lecturer’s permissions.","si":"Question එකේ “login succeeds, but access denied” කියන විට password check එක නොව resource permissions ගැන අවධානය දෙන්න."},"trap":{"en":"An identifier is a claim, not proof by itself.","si":"User ID එක කෙනෙකුට දැනගත හැකියි. ඒක දන්නා බව පමණක් එම user බවට සාක්ෂියක් නොවෙයි."}},{"id":"authentication-factors","title":"10.2 Four factor categories and MFA","pages":[8,9],"si":["Authentication සාක්ෂි වර්ග හතරක් ලෙස මේ lecture එකේ ඉගෙන ගන්නවා: දන්නා දෙයක්, තමන් සතුව තිබෙන දෙයක්, ශරීර ලක්ෂණයක්, හෝ හැසිරීමේ රටාවක්. Password එක Know; hardware token එක Have; fingerprint එක Are; typing rhythm එක Do ලෙස වර්ගීකරණය කරන්න.","MFA කියන්නේ password එකට අමතරව ඕනෑම දෙයක් නැවත අහන එක නොවෙයි. ස්වාධීන factor categories දෙකක් හෝ වැඩි ගණනක් අවශ්‍යයි. Password + PIN දෙකම Know නිසා ඒවා independent-factor MFA බවට පත් වෙන්නේ නැහැ."],"definition":{"term":"Multifactor Authentication","text":"Authentication that combines evidence from two or more distinct, appropriately independent factor categories."},"diagram":"mfa","table":{"headers":["Category","Examples","Typical limitation"],"rows":[["Something you know","Password, PIN, secret answer","Phishing, guessing or sharing"],["Something you have","Hardware token, smart card, registered authenticator","Loss, theft or compromise"],["Something you are","Fingerprint, face, retina","Spoofing, matching and privacy issues"],["Something you do","Typing rhythm, handwriting dynamics, voice pattern","Behavior can vary; matching errors may occur"]]},"example":{"q":"A portal checks a password, then asks for a second secret PIN. Is this definitely MFA?","steps":["Password is a knowledge factor.","PIN is also a knowledge factor.","The combination does not introduce a different factor category."],"answer":"No. Password and PIN are both Something You Know. Password plus a properly verified possession token is an example of knowledge plus possession and can provide MFA.","si":"රහස් දෙකක් තිබීම සහ factors දෙකක් තිබීම එකම දෙයක් නොවෙයි. විභාගයේ combination එකේ category දෙකම නමෙන් දක්වන්න."},"trap":{"en":"SSO and MFA are different properties and can be used together.","si":"SSO එක සේවා කිහිපයක login සම්බන්ධ කරන ආකාරයයි. MFA එක identity verify කිරීමට භාවිත කරන සාක්ෂි වර්ග ගැනයි."}},{"id":"password-attacks","title":"10.3 Recognize eight password attacks","pages":[10],"si":["Attack එක නම් කරන විට attacker කරන වැඩේ හඳුනාගන්න. එක් account එකකට ගොඩක් guesses යවනවාද? එකම common password එක accounts ගොඩකට යවනවාද? නැත්නම් සොරකම් කළ password verifiers තමන්ගේ computer එකේ test කරනවාද? මේ වෙනසෙන් නිවැරදි attack නම තෝරාගන්න පුළුවන්.","Online guessing වලදී requests login service එකට එන නිසා rate limiting වැනි controls උදව් වෙනවා. Offline guessing වලදී attacker තමන් සතුව ඇති verifiers පරීක්ෂා කරන නිසා live login page එකේ lockout එකෙන් ඒ වැඩේ නවත්වන්න බැහැ. එහිදී verifier database ආරක්ෂාව සහ slow salted password hashing වැදගත්."],"definition":{"term":"Online and offline password guessing","text":"Online guesses are submitted to the authentication service; offline guesses are tested locally against stolen password verifiers."},"table":{"headers":["Attack","Scenario clue","Suitable response"],"rows":[["Offline Dictionary","Stolen verifiers tested with a local wordlist","Protect verifiers; use suitable slow salted hashing"],["Specific Account","Many guesses against one account","Rate limits and appropriate temporary lockout"],["Popular Password / spraying","One common candidate across many accounts","MFA, breached-password screening and monitoring"],["Single-User Guessing","Personal facts used to predict a secret","Unpredictable unique passwords"],["Exploiting User Mistakes","Phishing, sharing or exposed passwords","Awareness plus stronger authentication where appropriate"],["Workstation Hijacking","Abuse of an unattended logged-in session","Automatic screen lock and session controls"],["Multiple Password Use","Same secret reused across services","Unique passwords and password-management support"],["Electronic Monitoring","Authentication data intercepted in transit","Authenticated encrypted connections and secure protocols"]]},"example":{"q":"An attacker steals a password database and runs a wordlist against the hashes locally. Name the attack and relevant controls.","steps":["The attacker already has the password verifiers.","Candidate passwords are tested without sending guesses to the live login service.","Select controls for offline guessing and database exposure."],"answer":"Offline Dictionary Attack. Protect the verifier database and use a suitable slow password-hashing function with unique salts and appropriate parameters. Login rate limiting helps online attacks but does not stop this attacker’s local guessing.","si":"“Stolen hashes” සහ “locally” කියන වචන offline attack එක හඳුනාගන්න උදව් වෙනවා. Login page එක lock කළත් attackerගේ copy එකට කරන guesses නවත්වන්න බැහැ."},"trap":{"en":"Password spraying targets many accounts with a small set of common candidates; it is not the same pattern as many guesses at one account.","si":"Account ගණන සහ guess කරන password ගණන වෙන වෙනම බලන්න."}},{"id":"password-verifiers","title":"10.4 Salted registration and secure verification","pages":[10,11,12],"si":["Password එක plaintext ලෙස database එකේ තබනවා වෙනුවට verifier එකක් තබනවා. Registration වෙලාවේ unique random salt එකක් හදා password එක, salt එක සහ අවශ්‍ය parameters යොදා slow password-hashing function එකකින් verifier එක ගන්නවා. Store කරන්නේ verifier එක සහ නැවත පරීක්ෂා කිරීමට අවශ්‍ය salt/parameters යි.","Login වෙලාවේ user ඇතුළත් කළ password එකට කලින් store කළ salt සහ ඒ parameters යොදා නැවත verifier එක ගණනය කරනවා. එය stored verifier එකට ගැළපුණොත් password check එක සාර්ථකයි. වෙනස් salts නිසා එකම password භාවිත කරන accounts දෙකක් සරලව hash equality එකෙන් හඳුනාගැනීම අමාරු වෙනවා."],"definition":{"term":"Salt and password verifier","text":"A salt is a unique random input used with the password when deriving a stored verifier. Verification recomputes a candidate verifier using the stored salt and parameters."},"diagram":"passwords","bullets":[{"en":"Registration: password + fresh salt + parameters → slow password-hashing function → verifier.","si":"Plaintext password එක ගබඩා නොකර verifier එක සහ salt/parameters තබන්න."},{"en":"Verification: entered password + stored salt/parameters → recompute → compare.","si":"Login වෙලාවේ අලුත් salt එකක් හදනවා වෙනුවට එම account එකේ store කළ salt එක භාවිත කරනවා."},{"en":"Salts reduce reuse of precomputed tables across different accounts.","si":"එක table එකක් සියලු salts සඳහා නැවත භාවිත කිරීම අමාරු කරනවා."},{"en":"The salt generally does not need secrecy.","si":"Salt එක තවත් රහස් password එකක් ලෙස සලකන්න එපා; password එකේ entropy එක වැඩි වුණා කියාත් නොලියන්න."}],"example":{"q":"Two employees choose the same password. Why should their stored verifiers differ?","steps":["Generate independent random salts S1 and S2.","Derive verifier V1 using the password and S1; derive V2 using the password and S2.","Store each verifier with its own salt and parameters."],"answer":"Different salts produce different password-hashing inputs and therefore distinct verifiers with overwhelming probability. This hides straightforward cross-account password equality and makes shared precomputation less reusable. A suitable slow password KDF also raises guessing cost.","si":"Password එක එකම වුණත් salt වෙනස් නම් function එකට යන සම්පූර්ණ input එක වෙනස්. ඒකෙන් hashes දෙක සමානද කියා බලලා එකම password බව සොයාගන්න ලේසි වෙන්නේ නැහැ."},"trap":{"en":"A salt does not prevent an attacker from testing guesses against a known-salt verifier.","si":"Salt එක දන්නා නිසාත් guesses පරීක්ෂා කළ හැකියි. එම guesses මිල අධික කිරීමට slow password hashing එකත් අවශ්‍යයි."},"supplement":"Practical clarification from the guide: the diagram is a teaching model. Password storage should use a suitable password-hashing algorithm and parameters, rather than a plain fast SHA-256 hash. The guide gives Argon2id as an example; this page explains the concept rather than prescribing implementation settings."},{"id":"single-sign-on","title":"10.5 SSO: one identity service, several applications","pages":[12],"si":["SSO එකෙන් Courseweb, Library සහ Student Portal වැනි සම්බන්ධ සේවා සඳහා එක මධ්‍යම authentication arrangement එකක් භාවිත කරන්න පුළුවන්. හැම සේවාවකටම වෙන වෙනම password මතක තබාගැනීමේ බර අඩු වෙනවා. Accounts ලබාදීම සහ ඉවත් කිරීමත් මධ්‍යගතව පාලනය කිරීම පහසු වෙන්න පුළුවන්.","ඒ සමඟ අවදානමත් එක තැනකට එකතු වෙනවා. Identity provider එක compromise වුණොත් සම්බන්ධ සේවා කිහිපයකට බලපාන්න පුළුවන්. එය unavailable වුණොත් අලුත් sign-ins බාධා විය හැකියි. ඒ නිසා MFA, secure sessions, monitoring සහ identity service එකේ resilience වැදගත්."],"definition":{"term":"Single Sign-On","text":"An authentication arrangement in which a central sign-in can support access to several associated applications, while each application still enforces its authorization rules."},"diagram":"sso","table":{"headers":["Benefit","Related limitation / control"],"rows":[["Fewer separate credentials","Central-account compromise can have a wider impact; use strong authentication"],["Central account administration","Protect provisioning and revocation processes"],["Less repetitive login","Protect session tokens and session lifecycle"],["Shared identity service","Plan for provider availability and integration complexity"]]},"example":{"q":"A university connects Courseweb, its Library Portal and Student Portal to one identity provider. Does this mean a student may edit marks in every application?","steps":["Central authentication can support access to associated applications.","The student’s role and permissions are still distinct from a lecturer’s.","Each application must authorize the requested operation."],"answer":"No. SSO centralizes authentication, not unrestricted permissions. Each application must enforce the student’s authorized actions. Protect the shared identity with appropriate MFA, monitoring and session controls.","si":"එක login එකකින් services කිහිපයකට යාම, ඒ services සියල්ලේම admin වීමක් නොවෙයි. SSO සහ authorization වෙන වෙනම පැහැදිලි කරන්න."},"trap":{"en":"SSO reduces repeated authentication; it does not replace per-resource authorization.","si":"One sign-in කියන්නේ all permissions කියන අර්ථය නොවෙයි."}},{"id":"challenge-response","title":"10.6 Nonces, challenge–response and replay","pages":[13],"si":["Replay attack එකකදී attacker කලින් වලංගු වූ response එකක් අල්ලාගෙන පසුව නැවත යවනවා. Server එක හැම අවස්ථාවකටම fresh challenge එකක් දුන්නොත්, අද අවශ්‍ය response එක ඊයේ response එකට වඩා වෙනස් වෙනවා. Nonce කියන්නේ මෙසේ නැවත භාවිත නොකරන අලුත් value එකයි.","Client එක challenge එක සහ secret එකට සම්බන්ධ සාක්ෂියක් භාවිත කර response එක හදනවා. Server එක මේ challenge එකට බලාපොරොත්තු වන response එක verify කරනවා. කලින් recording එක නැවත එවීමෙන් current challenge එකට ගැළපෙන response එකක් සාමාන්‍යයෙන් ලැබෙන්නේ නැහැ. ඒත් freshness එක පමණක් තිබීමෙන් protocol එකේ සියලු ආරක්ෂක ගැටලු විසඳෙන්නේ නැහැ."],"definition":{"term":"Challenge–response authentication","text":"The verifier sends a fresh challenge and checks a secret-dependent response bound to that challenge, reducing reuse of previously recorded responses."},"diagram":"challenge","bullets":[{"en":"Client identifies the account.","si":"Account එකට අදාළ authentication පරීක්ෂාව තෝරාගන්න identity එක දෙනවා."},{"en":"Server sends a fresh unpredictable nonce.","si":"කලින් response එක නැවත භාවිත කළ නොහැකි අලුත් challenge එකක් දෙනවා."},{"en":"Client derives a response using the challenge and authentication secret.","si":"Secret එක සරලව යැවීම වෙනුවට එයට සම්බන්ධ response එකක් හදනවා."},{"en":"Server verifies the expected response for this challenge.","si":"කලින් challenge එකක response එක නොව දැන් දුන් challenge එකට ගැළපෙන response එක බලනවා."}],"example":{"q":"Yesterday’s valid response is replayed today, but the server has issued a different nonce. Why should authentication fail?","steps":["The recorded response belongs to the earlier challenge.","The verifier now expects a response bound to a fresh challenge.","Reject a response that fails this current challenge check."],"answer":"The old response should not verify for the new nonce, so the replay is rejected. The protocol must correctly bind the response to the challenge and enforce freshness; a nonce alone does not guarantee security against all attacks.","si":"ඊයේ response එක ඊයේ ප්‍රශ්නයට දුන් උත්තරයක් වගේ. අද server එක අලුත් challenge එකක් දුන්නාම ඒ පරණ response එක ගැළපෙන්නෙ නැහැ."},"trap":{"en":"A fresh nonce does not automatically prevent phishing, man-in-the-middle attacks or offline guessing in an insecure construction.","si":"Replay අඩු කළා කියලා අනෙක් සියලු attacks නවතිනවා යැයි නොලියන්න."},"supplement":"Protocol clarification: the guide’s R = f(r, h(P)) formula is illustrative. A real authentication protocol must be vetted; exposing password-equivalent material or allowing offline guessing can defeat an otherwise fresh exchange."}],"checkpoint":[{"q":"Why is password plus PIN not automatically MFA?","a":"Both belong to the Something You Know category.","si":"සාක්ෂි දෙකම එකම factor category එකට අයත්."},{"q":"Which attack tests stolen password verifiers locally?","a":"Offline Dictionary Attack.","si":"Live login service එකට guesses යවන්නේ නැති නිසා offline."},{"q":"What is a main advantage of SSO?","a":"One central authentication arrangement supports several associated applications.","si":"වෙන වෙනම login සහ password කළමනාකරණයේ බර අඩු වෙනවා."},{"q":"Give two purposes of a unique salt.","a":"Hide straightforward same-password verifier equality and reduce reuse of precomputed attacks across salts.","si":"Salt එක password රහසක් නොවෙයි; වෙන් වූ verifier inputs ලබාදීමයි එහි වැදගත් කාර්යය."},{"q":"Which attack is reduced by a correctly used fresh nonce?","a":"Replay Attack.","si":"කලින් වලංගු response එක අලුත් challenge එකට නොගැළපෙන ලෙස පරීක්ෂා කරනවා."}],"summary":"Week 10 සඳහා password registration flow එකත් login verification flow එකත් වෙන වෙනම අඳින්න. MFA ගැන අහන විට factor categories දෙකම ලියන්න. Challenge–Response ගැන අහන විට fresh nonce, secret-dependent response සහ verification යන පියවර පැහැදිලි කරන්න."},{"week":11,"title":"Disaster Recovery & Business Continuity","subtitle":"සේවාව නවතිද්දීත් අත්‍යවශ්‍ය වැඩ කරගෙන යමු","pages":[15,20],"intro":"පද්ධතියක් බිඳවැටුණාම ප්‍රශ්න දෙකක් විසඳන්න වෙනවා: දැන්ම අත්‍යවශ්‍ය සේවාව පවත්වාගන්නේ කොහොමද, සහ සාමාන්‍ය පද්ධතිය නැවත ගොඩනගන්නේ කොහොමද? Business Continuity පළමු ප්‍රශ්නයටත් Disaster Recovery දෙවන ප්‍රශ්නයටත් වැඩි අවධානයක් දෙනවා.","objectives":["Distinguish business continuity from disaster recovery.","Read the recovery timeline and calculate its separate intervals.","Compare recovery strategies without confusing redundancy with backup.","Explain BCP phases, responsibilities and provider selection."],"topics":[{"id":"dr-bc","title":"11.1 Availability: DRP versus BCP","pages":[15],"si":["University portal එකේ database server එක ගින්නකින් අක්‍රිය වුණා කියලා හිතන්න. එය නැවත සාදා data restore කිරීම Disaster Recovery වැඩක්. එතෙක් වෙනත් portal එකකින් අත්‍යවශ්‍ය අධ්‍යයන සේවා ලබාදීම Business Continuity වැඩක්.","දෙකම Availability රැකගැනීමට උපකාරී වෙනවා. නමුත් BCP එක IT equipment වලට පමණක් සීමා නැහැ: මිනිසුන්, ක්‍රියාපටිපාටි, සැපයුම්කරුවන් සහ අවශ්‍ය සන්නිවේදනයත් එයට අයත්. DRP එක එම පුළුල් සැලැස්මට සහාය වන system/data recovery කොටසයි."],"definition":{"term":"DRP and BCP","text":"Disaster recovery restores disrupted systems, data and infrastructure. Business continuity maintains essential business services during a disruption."},"diagram":"dr-bc","table":{"headers":["Disaster recovery","Business continuity"],"rows":[["Restore failed systems and data","Continue essential business activities"],["Recover the damaged database","Operate a temporary admissions or banking service"],["IT restoration is a main focus","People, processes, suppliers and technology all matter"]]},"example":{"q":"A bank starts processing at a backup site at noon and rebuilds the damaged main database that evening. Identify the BC and DR activities.","steps":["The backup site keeps essential customer transactions operating.","Rebuilding the main database restores the failed normal infrastructure."],"answer":"Backup-site processing is business continuity; restoring the damaged main database is disaster recovery. Both support availability.","si":"“වැඩ දිගටම කරනවාද?” නම් BC. “බිඳවැටුණු දේ නැවත හදනවාද?” නම් DR. එකම සිද්ධියේ ක්‍රියා දෙකම තිබෙන්න පුළුවන්."},"trap":{"en":"Do not define BCP as only restoring servers.","si":"BCP එකේ අරමුණ ව්‍යාපාරයේ අත්‍යවශ්‍ය වැඩ පවත්වාගැනීමයි; server repair කිරීම පමණක් නොවෙයි."}},{"id":"timeline","title":"11.2 Read the recovery timeline","pages":[16],"si":["Failure එකෙන් පසු අත්‍යවශ්‍ය සේවාව ආපසු පටන්ගන්න තෙක් තියෙන ආරම්භක කාලය Initial Interruption ලෙස බලන්න. සේවාව තාවකාලික පද්ධතියකින් සීමිත මට්ටමකින් කරන කාලය Alternate Mode. සියලු සාමාන්‍ය සේවා නැවත ලැබුණාම Full Restoration සිදුවෙනවා.","SDO කියන්නේ Alternate Mode තුළ බලාපොරොත්තු වන සේවා මට්ටමයි. උදාහරණයක් ලෙස balance බැලීම සහ හදිසි transfers පමණක් ලබාදෙන්න පුළුවන්. වේලාවක් ගණනය කරන විට failure → alternate service සහ alternate service → full restoration වෙන වෙනම ගණනය කරන්න."],"definition":{"term":"Recovery timeline","text":"Initial interruption is the interval before essential service resumes. Alternate mode maintains a defined service level until normal operations are fully restored."},"diagram":"timeline","table":{"headers":["Term","Meaning in this guide","Remember"],"rows":[["Interruption Window","Acceptable waiting time before an essential service resumes","A business tolerance, not automatically the actual outage"],["Alternate Mode","Temporary operating arrangement for essential services","Service can be reduced"],["SDO","Service Delivery Objective","Target service level during Alternate Mode"],["MTO","Maximum Tolerable Outage; explain the lecture’s stated context","The source slide and timeline use different wording"]]},"example":{"q":"Failure occurs at 08:00, alternate service resumes at 09:30, and full restoration completes at 15:00. Calculate the two intervals.","steps":["08:00 → 09:30 = 1 hour 30 minutes of initial interruption.","09:30 → 15:00 = 5 hours 30 minutes in Alternate Mode.","Failure → full restoration is 7 hours, a separate total."],"answer":"Initial interruption: 1 h 30 min. Alternate-mode duration: 5 h 30 min. Total failure-to-restoration time: 7 h.","si":"09:30 කියන්නේ කාල දෙක වෙන්වන සීමාවයි. මුළු පැය 7ම interruption ලෙස නොලියන්න; තාවකාලික සේවාව ආරම්භ වූ පසු ව්‍යාපාරය සම්පූර්ණයෙන් නතර වී නැහැ."},"trap":{"en":"MTO wording in the lecture is not fully consistent. State the interval you mean.","si":"Guide එකේ page 16 අනුව slide එක “Maximum time in Alternate Mode” කියන නමුත් timeline bracket එක disruption සිට restoration දක්වා පෙන්වනවා. පිළිතුරේ ඔබ අදහස් කරන කාල සීමාව පැහැදිලි කරන්න."},"supplement":"Supplementary terminology: RTO is a target time for recovery; RPO expresses tolerable data loss as a time interval. These are useful background terms, but this guide explicitly treats them as supplementary to the uploaded lecture."},{"id":"recovery-sites","title":"11.3 Choose a recovery strategy","pages":[17],"si":["Recovery site එකේ කලින් සූදානම් කර තිබෙන දේ වැඩි වන තරමට සාමාන්‍යයෙන් recovery එක වේගවත් වෙනවා. ඒ සඳහා වැඩි වියදමක් දරන්න වෙනවා. Cold Site එකේ මූලික තැන සහ පහසුකම් තිබුණත් equipment/configuration/data restoration සඳහා වැඩි සූදානමක් අවශ්‍යයි.","Warm Site එක අර්ධ වශයෙන් සූදානම්. Hot Site එකේ equipment, software සහ network වඩාත් සූදානම්. Mirrored Site එක primary environment සහ data සමීපව පිටපත් කර පවත්වාගන්නවා. වේගය අවශ්‍යද, data loss කොපමණ දරාගත හැකිද, සහ budget එක කොපමණද කියා බලලා තෝරන්න."],"definition":{"term":"Recovery strategies","text":"A recovery strategy balances service criticality, recovery readiness, acceptable downtime, data protection and cost."},"diagram":"recovery-sites","table":{"headers":["Approach","What is ready?","Typical trade-off"],"rows":[["Cold Site","Facility and basic infrastructure; equipment/setup still needed","Lower ongoing cost; slower recovery"],["Warm Site","Some equipment and configuration","Moderate preparation and cost"],["Hot Site","Prepared compatible hardware, software and connectivity","Faster recovery; higher cost"],["Mirrored Site","Closely duplicated infrastructure and replicated data","Very high readiness; high cost"],["Mutual Backup","Compatible organizations agree to provide facilities to each other","Depends on partner capacity, readiness and shared disaster exposure"],["Remote Journaling","Transaction records or data changes are sent remotely","Data-loss exposure depends on timing and architecture"]]},"example":{"q":"An online hospital records service has very low downtime tolerance and a substantial recovery budget. Which strategy may fit?","steps":["Identify the critical need for rapid access to records.","Compare well-prepared Hot and Mirrored Sites with the recovery objectives.","Evaluate replication freshness, failover capacity and protected backups."],"answer":"A suitably designed Hot or Mirrored Site may fit. A Mirrored Site can support very rapid recovery when replication and failover are properly engineered; the actual choice depends on recovery objectives and budget.","si":"“වැඩි budget එකක්” තිබුණා කියලා නමක් පමණක් තෝරන්න එපා. අවශ්‍ය recovery time, data freshness සහ actual failover හැකියාව එයට ගැළපෙන බව කියන්න."},"trap":{"en":"Mirroring does not remove the need for independent protected backups.","si":"වැරදි වෙනස්කමක් හෝ corruption එකක් replica එකටත් යා හැකි නිසා වෙනම protected backups සහ restore testing අවශ්‍යයි."}},{"id":"resilience","title":"11.4 Redundancy is one layer of resilience","pages":[18],"si":["RAID එකකින් disk කිහිපයක් භාවිත කර local disk failure එකකට ඔරොත්තු දෙන්න පුළුවන්. නමුත් site එකම ගින්නකින් විනාශ වුණොත්, ransomware එකෙන් files වෙනස් වුණොත්, හෝ වැරදිව delete කළොත් RAID එක පමණක් recovery පිළිතුරක් නොවෙයි.","Fault-tolerant servers, distributed processing සහ SAN වැනි ක්‍රම availability වැඩි කළ හැකියි. ඒවායේ shared power, storage, network සහ site dependencies තවම තිබිය හැකියි. “පිටපතක් තිබෙනවා” සහ “අනතුරකින් පසු පරීක්ෂා කළ recovery එකක් කළ හැකියි” යන දෙක වෙන් කර තේරුම් ගන්න."],"definition":{"term":"High availability and redundancy","text":"Redundancy provides additional components or processing capacity to reduce specific failures. Disaster recovery also requires protected data, independent recovery arrangements and tested procedures."},"diagram":"resilience","table":{"headers":["Technology","Purpose","What it does not replace"],"rows":[["RAID","Local disk redundancy","Off-site backup and the wider disaster recovery plan"],["Fault-Tolerant Server","Service can move to backup components or a backup server","Site-level resilience by itself"],["Distributed Processing","Workload is spread across several nodes","Cross-site recovery unless specifically designed"],["Storage Area Network (SAN)","Networked shared storage and data movement","Backup policy and restoration testing"]]},"example":{"q":"A company has RAID storage but no separate backups. A ransomware incident corrupts its records. Is RAID sufficient?","steps":["RAID targets certain hardware/disk failures.","Ransomware may change the live data across the array.","Recovering trustworthy records requires suitable protected backups and tested restoration."],"answer":"No. RAID alone is not a complete backup or disaster recovery strategy. Maintain separate protected copies and verify that they can be restored.","si":"Array එකේ disks කිහිපයකම එකම corrupted data තිබුණොත් හොඳ copy එකක් ලැබෙන්නේ නැහැ. Recovery සඳහා ආරක්ෂිත, ප්‍රයෝජනයට ගත හැකි වෙනම පිටපතක් අවශ්‍යයි."},"trap":{"en":"More disks do not automatically mean protection against every kind of data loss.","si":"උපාංග redundancy සහ data recovery දෙක වෙනම අවශ්‍යතා ලෙස සලකන්න."}},{"id":"bcp-phases","title":"11.5 Build, test and maintain the continuity plan","pages":[18,19],"si":["BCP එක IT team එක ලියලා තබන document එකක් පමණක් නොවෙයි. Executives, managers, business departments සහ employees එයට සහභාගී වෙන්න ඕන. BC/DR Coordinator කෙනෙකුට සම්බන්ධීකරණය, reviews, updated copies බෙදාහැරීම සහ සැලැස්ම පවත්වාගෙන යාමේ වගකීම් තිබෙනවා.","අනුපිළිවෙළ හය මතක තබාගන්න: Project Initiation → Business/Risk Analysis → Design & Development → Implementation → Testing → Maintenance. Testing එකෙන් සැලැස්ම ඇත්තටම ක්‍රියා කරනවාද බලනවා. Maintenance එකෙන් මිනිසුන්, systems සහ අවදානම් වෙනස් වන විට plan එක යාවත්කාලීන කරනවා."],"definition":{"term":"Business Continuity Planning","text":"BCP is an ongoing organizational process for maintaining essential operations, with defined responsibilities, resources, exercises and updates."},"diagram":"bcp-phases","table":{"headers":["Phase","What happens"],"rows":[["1. Project Initiation","Define scope, objectives, sponsorship and planning committee"],["2. Business/Risk Analysis","Identify risks, business impacts, recovery options and budget"],["3. Design & Development","Design teams, responsibilities and action plans"],["4. Implementation","Arrange resources, contracts and operating procedures"],["5. Testing","Run simulations or exercises; record results and weaknesses"],["6. Maintenance","Review changes, improve the plan and redistribute current copies"]]},"bullets":[{"en":"Life safety and evacuation","si":"මුලින් මිනිසුන්ගේ ආරක්ෂාව සලකා බලන්න."},{"en":"Disaster declaration criteria and authority","si":"Recovery activate කරන්නේ කවුද සහ කුමන තත්ත්වයකදීද කියා ලියන්න."},{"en":"Responsibilities, contacts and resource allocation","si":"අනතුරකදී කවුරු මොන වැඩ කරන්නේද, අවශ්‍ය resources ලැබෙන්නේ කොහෙන්ද කියා පැහැදිලි කරන්න."},{"en":"Recovery and alternate-mode procedures","si":"Failed systems restore කරන ආකාරයත් එතෙක් අත්‍යවශ්‍ය වැඩ කරන ආකාරයත් දෙකම ඇතුළත් කරන්න."},{"en":"Off-site plan copies","si":"Primary site එක භාවිත කළ නොහැකි විටත් සැලැස්ම ලබාගත හැකි විය යුතුයි."}],"example":{"q":"The organization simulates a data-center outage, records delays, and later updates contact details after staff changes. Name the relevant phases.","steps":["The simulation evaluates whether the procedures work: Testing.","Changing the plan after people or systems change is Maintenance."],"answer":"The outage exercise is Testing. Updating contacts and procedures after changes is Maintenance; both are ongoing rather than one-time activities.","si":"Plan එක ලියූ දවසෙන් වැඩේ ඉවර වෙන්නේ නැහැ. Exercise එකෙන් දුර්වලකම් හොයාගෙන, වෙනස්කම් අනුව එය නැවත සකස් කරන්න ඕන."},"trap":{"en":"A written plan that has never been tested is not proof of recovery capability.","si":"කඩදාසියේ තිබෙන පියවර ඇත්තටම කළ හැකිද කියා exercise එකකින් පරීක්ෂා කරන්න."}},{"id":"provider","title":"11.6 Evaluate a third-party recovery provider","pages":[19],"si":["Backup center එකක් කුලියට ගන්න කලින් floor space තිබෙනවාද කියන එක පමණක් බලන්න එපා. Failover වෙලාවේ සැබෑ transaction volume එක handle කරන්න equipment, storage, network capacity සහ skilled staff තිබෙනවාද කියා පරීක්ෂා කරන්න.","Vendor support, budget, compatible systems සහ providerගේ recovery readiness එකත් වැදගත්. ප්‍රශ්නයක “factors දෙකක්” ඉල්ලුවොත් නාම දෙකක් පමණක් නොව, එක් එක් factor එක අවශ්‍ය ඇයි කියා scenario එකට සම්බන්ධ කර ලියන්න."],"definition":{"term":"Recovery provider selection","text":"Choose a recovery provider whose facilities, capacity, connectivity, support and skilled personnel can support the organization’s actual recovery requirements."},"diagram":"provider","table":{"headers":["Factor","Why it matters"],"rows":[["Floor Space","Enough suitable room for the recovery equipment and staff"],["Redundant Equipment","Sufficient compatible processing and storage when normal systems fail"],["Redundant Network Capacity","Connectivity can carry the real workload and survive relevant failures"],["Vendor Support","Help is available when recovery is activated"],["Budget","The service and recovery option are sustainable"],["Skilled Personnel","People can operate, restore and troubleshoot the required systems"]]},"example":{"q":"A rented recovery site cannot handle the normal transaction volume during failover. Identify two poorly evaluated factors.","steps":["Check whether processing/storage equipment has adequate capacity.","Check whether network bandwidth and supporting infrastructure can carry the workload."],"answer":"Insufficient equipment/processing capacity and insufficient network capacity were poorly assessed. The provider must demonstrate capacity under the expected failover workload.","si":"Site එක තිබුණත් customersගේ වැඩ ප්‍රමාණය දරාගන්න බැරි නම් continuity ඉලක්කය ඉටු වෙන්නේ නැහැ. Capacity එක actual workload එකට සම්බන්ධ කර පරීක්ෂා කළ යුතුයි."},"supplement":"Practical clarification: test restoration and failover with representative workloads; a promise of available space alone does not demonstrate service readiness."}],"checkpoint":[{"q":"DR or BC: rebuilding a failed main server?","a":"Disaster recovery.","si":"බිඳවැටුණු infrastructure නැවත ගොඩනගන නිසා DR."},{"q":"DR or BC: serving customers from a temporary site?","a":"Business continuity.","si":"Normal site එක නැති අතරත් අත්‍යවශ්‍ය සේවාව දිගටම කරන නිසා BC."},{"q":"Which is normally slower to recover: a Cold Site or a Hot Site?","a":"A Cold Site, because more setup and restoration are required.","si":"Cold site එකේ කලින් සූදානම් කර තිබෙන දේ අඩුයි."},{"q":"What happens during BCP Testing?","a":"Exercises or simulations evaluate procedures, readiness and results.","si":"Plan එක ඇත්තටම ක්‍රියා කරනවාද සහ දුර්වලකම් මොනවාද කියා බලනවා."},{"q":"Why does RAID not replace protected backups?","a":"RAID does not cover all deletion, corruption, ransomware or site loss.","si":"Disk redundancy තිබුණත් සෑම data-loss හේතුවකින්ම ආරක්ෂාව නොලැබෙයි."}],"summary":"DR = restore; BC = continue. Timeline එකේ initial interruption සහ alternate duration වෙන් කරන්න. Recovery readiness වැඩි කිරීමට වියදමක් ඇති බවත් mirroring/RAID වෙනම backups වෙනුවට භාවිත නොකළ යුතු බවත් මතක තබාගන්න. BCP phases හය අනුපිළිවෙළින් ලියා, Testing සහ Maintenance අවශ්‍ය ඇයි කියා පැහැදිලි කරන්න."},{"week":12,"title":"Firewalls, ACLs & Network Security","subtitle":"Packet එක යන්නේ කොහෙන්ද, කොතැනටද, අවසර තිබේද?","pages":[21,28],"intro":"Firewall එක network එකේ electronic checkpoint එකක් වගේ. Packet එකේ තොරතුරු සහ policy එක සසඳා allow හෝ deny කරනවා. Network security තේරුම් ගන්න හොඳම ක්‍රමය source, destination, ports සහ rule order එකට පියවරෙන් පියවර packet එකක් trace කරන එකයි.","objectives":["Trace a packet through first-match ACL rules.","Distinguish stateless filtering from stateful inspection.","Draw a screened-subnet DMZ and explain its limits.","Compare detection, prevention, log correlation and VPN tunnelling."],"topics":[{"id":"packet","title":"12.1 Firewall fundamentals and packet fields","pages":[21],"si":["Packet එකකට “හොඳ” හෝ “නරක” කියලා නමක් ලියලා නැහැ. Firewall එක Source IP, Destination IP, Source Port, Destination Port සහ Protocol වගේ fields පරීක්ෂා කර තම policy එකට අනුව තීරණය කරනවා. Source කියන්නේ ආරම්භය; Destination කියන්නේ එය යන තැන.","Layer 3දී IP addresses වැදගත්. Layer 4දී TCP/UDP සහ ports වැදගත්. Application-aware controls වලට protocol behavior හෝ content ගැන වැඩි අවබෝධයක් තිබිය හැකියි. Interface එකට සාපේක්ෂ IN/OUT direction එකත් බලන්න; reply packet එකේ source/destination fields මුල් request එකේ ඒවාට වෙනස් වෙනවා."],"definition":{"term":"Firewall","text":"A firewall is a hardware or software security system that controls traffic into or out of a protected network according to defined security rules."},"diagram":"packet","table":{"headers":["Service","Port / protocol","Context"],"rows":[["HTTP","TCP 80","Public web requests in the lecture"],["SMTP","TCP 25","Email delivery in the lecture"],["SSH","TCP 22","Supplementary management example"],["HTTPS","TCP 443","Supplementary encrypted-web example"]]},"bullets":[{"en":"Layer 3: addresses","si":"Packet එක ආරම්භ වන්නේ සහ යන්නේ මොන IP addresses අතරද බලන්න."},{"en":"Layer 4: protocol and ports","si":"TCP/UDP සහ source/destination port fields වෙන වෙනම පරීක්ෂා කරන්න."},{"en":"Application layer: behavior/content","si":"Basic header filtering එකකට නොපෙනෙන application context එකක් වැඩි මට්ටමේ controls බලන්න පුළුවන්."},{"en":"Secondary functions","si":"සමහර firewall products NAT, VPN හෝ proxy services ද ලබාදෙනවා. ඒ එකිනෙක වෙනස් කාර්යයක් කරන නිසා firewalling සමඟ පටලවාගන්න එපා."}],"example":{"q":"A TCP request goes from 10.1.0.3:50000 to 198.51.100.8:80. Identify the client-side ephemeral port and the web-service port.","steps":["Source IP/port: 10.1.0.3:50000.","Destination IP/port: 198.51.100.8:80.","The destination service in this example is HTTP."],"answer":"50000 is the client-side source port; 80 is the destination web-service port. For a reply, these endpoint roles reverse.","si":"Port 80 තිබෙන පැත්ත බලන එක පමණක් නොව එය source ද destination ද කියා හඳුනාගන්න. Reply එකේ source port එක 80 විය හැකියි."},"trap":{"en":"A port number is a rule-matching field, not proof that traffic is safe.","si":"Attack එකක් allowed port එකක් හරහාත් ගමන් කළ හැකියි."}},{"id":"acl","title":"12.2 First-match ACLs: trace every field","pages":[21,22,23],"si":["ACL එක ordered rules list එකක්. මේ lecture model එකේ Rule A සිට පහළට පරීක්ෂා කර පළමු matching rule එකේ Allow/Deny තීරණය භාවිත කරනවා. තීරණයක් ගත්තට පසු පහළ matching rules බලන්නේ නැහැ. ඒ නිසා specific deny එක broad allow එකට පසුව දැමුවොත් එය වැඩ නොකරන්න පුළුවන්.","Stealth Rule එක firewall එකටම යන අනවසර traffic සීමා කරනවා. Cleanup Rule එක කලින් කිසිදු allow එකකින් අවසර නොලැබුණු traffic අවසානයේ deny කරනවා. මෙහි internal subnet එක 10.1.0.0/16; firewall IP එක 10.1.0.1. Source port සහ destination port පටලවාගන්න එපා."],"definition":{"term":"Network ACL","text":"A network ACL is an ordered set of permit/deny rules. In this lecture’s first-match model, processing stops at the first matching rule."},"diagram":"acl","table":{"headers":["Rule","Source","S.Port","Destination","D.Port","Proto","Action"],"rows":[["A","Any","Any","10.1.0.1","Any","Any","Deny"],["B","10.1.0.0/16","Any","10.2.12.12","Any","Any","Deny"],["C","10.1.0.0/16","Any","Any","80","TCP","Allow"],["D","Any","80","10.1.0.0/16","Any","TCP","Allow"],["E","Any","Any","10.1.1.2","25","TCP","Allow"],["F","10.1.1.2","25","Any","Any","TCP","Allow"],["G","Any","Any","10.1.0.20","80","TCP","Allow"],["H","10.1.0.20","80","Any","Any","TCP","Allow"],["I","Any","Any","Any","Any","Any","Deny"]]},"example":{"q":"Trace three TCP packets: (a) 10.1.0.3:50000 → 10.2.12.12:80; (b) 198.51.100.8:80 → 10.1.0.3:50000; (c) 203.0.113.8:50000 → 10.1.0.5:22.","steps":["(a) A does not match; B matches the internal source and blocked destination. Stop at B.","(b) Not A/B/C; D matches source port 80 and the internal destination. Stop at D.","(c) No specific allow matches SSH to this internal host. Reach final Rule I."],"answer":"(a) Rule B: DENY. (b) Rule D: ALLOW in the stateless lecture table. (c) Rule I: DENY. Later rules do not override an earlier match.","si":"(a) HTTP වුණත් blocked destination එක නිසා B එකෙන් නවතිනවා. (b) D එක source port 80 බලන broad return rule එකයි. (c) අවසර දෙන rule එකක් නැති නිසා cleanup rule එක ක්‍රියා කරනවා."},"trap":{"en":"The source-port-80 return rule is a lecture example, not proof of a genuine reply.","si":"Rule D එක allow වුණා කියලා packet එක කලින් ඉල්ලූ reply එකක් බව තහවුරු වෙන්නේ නැහැ. ඒ වෙනස stateful inspection කොටසේ බලන්න."},"supplement":"Source fidelity: This A–I table is reproduced exactly from PDF page 22. “Any” matches the lecture wildcard; /16 makes the protected subnet explicit. It is a teaching model, not a complete production firewall policy."},{"id":"stateful","title":"12.3 Stateless filtering versus stateful inspection","pages":[23,24],"si":["Stateless filter එක packet එකක් තනිවම header rules අනුව බලනවා. Stateful firewall එක allowed connection එකක් ගැන state මතක තබාගන්නවා. ඒ නිසා incoming packet එක tracked connection එකට ගැළපෙන reply එකක්ද කියා තවත් context එකක් සමඟ පරීක්ෂා කළ හැකියි.","TCP handshake එක SYN → SYN-ACK → ACK ලෙස යනවා. Stateful inspection එකට මේ connection progress ගැන අවබෝධයක් තිබිය හැකියි. නමුත් allowed connection එකක් කියලා application content එක සෑමවිටම ආරක්ෂිත බව හෝ endpoint එක හොඳ බව ඔප්පු වෙන්නේ නැහැ."],"definition":{"term":"Stateful Packet Inspection","text":"Stateful inspection evaluates traffic in the context of tracked authorized connections rather than relying only on independent packet-header matches."},"diagram":"stateful","table":{"headers":["Stateless","Stateful"],"rows":[["Evaluate each packet independently","Track connection/session state"],["Return traffic can require explicit broad rules","Recognize return traffic consistent with allowed state"],["Source port alone gives limited context","Validate packet direction and connection progress"],["Simpler rule processing model","Maintains state and consumes state resources"]]},"example":{"q":"A packet claims source port 80 but no corresponding allowed connection exists. Why is “port 80 means web reply” inadequate?","steps":["An attacker can choose or forge packet-header values.","A stateless source-port rule does not establish a prior request.","Stateful inspection checks consistency with an authorized tracked flow."],"answer":"Source port 80 alone does not prove that the packet is a legitimate HTTP response. A stateful firewall can reject traffic inconsistent with tracked authorized session state.","si":"“Reply එකක් වගේ පෙනෙනවා” සහ “අපි කලින් ආරම්භ කළ connection එකකට ගැළපෙනවා” කියන්නේ දෙකක්. State table එක දෙවැනි කරුණ පරීක්ෂා කිරීමට උපකාරී වෙනවා."},"trap":{"en":"Stateful inspection is not a guarantee against every attack over an allowed connection.","si":"Firewall state එක තිබුණත් vulnerable web application එකකට වෙනම application security controls අවශ්‍යයි."}},{"id":"dmz","title":"12.4 Architecture: filtering router, bastion host and DMZ","pages":[24,25],"si":["Internet එකෙන් සැමට භාවිත කළ යුතු web/email server එක sensitive payroll හෝ patient database එකේ network එකටම unrestricted ලෙස සම්බන්ධ කිරීම අවදානම්. DMZ එක public-facing services සඳහා වෙන් කළ network zone එකක්. Internal database එක තවත් restrictive firewall හෝ segment එකකින් ආරක්ෂා කරනවා.","Simple topology එක filtering router එකකින් internal LAN එක ආරක්ෂා කරනවා. Screened-host design එක filtering router සහ hardened bastion host එකක් භාවිත කරනවා. Screened-subnet DMZ එකකින් public servers සහ internal resources අතර තවත් පැහැදිලි සීමාවක් ලබාදෙන්න පුළුවන්. DMZ → database access අවශ්‍ය ප්‍රමාණයට පමණක් සීමා කරන්න."],"definition":{"term":"DMZ and bastion host","text":"A DMZ is a separate screened network for public-facing services. A bastion host is a hardened exposed system used for controlled gateway or public-facing functions."},"diagram":"dmz","table":{"headers":["Architecture","Main idea"],"rows":[["Simple topology","Filtering router controls access to the internal LAN"],["Screened host","Filtering router works with a hardened bastion host"],["Screened subnet / DMZ","Public services are isolated between outside and sensitive internal networks"]]},"example":{"q":"A hospital has a public appointment website and a confidential patient database. Where should the website go?","steps":["The website needs external access, so place it in a DMZ.","Keep the patient database in a protected internal segment.","Permit only specifically required website-to-database connections."],"answer":"Place the public website in a DMZ and the patient database in the protected internal network. Restrictive firewall rules reduce unnecessary direct access and limit lateral movement if the public server is compromised.","si":"Public website එකට Internet access අවශ්‍යයි; එම අවශ්‍යතාව නිසා database එකත් public කරන්න අවශ්‍ය නැහැ. අවශ්‍ය application connection පමණක් inner firewall එකෙන් allow කරන්න."},"trap":{"en":"A DMZ reduces exposure; it does not remove application vulnerabilities or rule-configuration errors.","si":"DMZ server එක patch කිරීම, application testing සහ least-privilege rules තවම අවශ්‍යයි."}},{"id":"detection","title":"12.5 Detect, prevent and correlate","pages":[25,26],"si":["IDS එක සැක සහිත activity හඳුනාගෙන alert දෙනවා. IPS එකට එවැනි traffic block කිරීම හෝ connection නතර කිරීමත් කළ හැකියි. SIEM එක විවිධ systems වල logs එකට ගෙන සම්බන්ධ කර බලනවා. UTM එක firewall, malware filtering සහ intrusion-related controls වැනි සේවා කිහිපයක් එකම solution එකක එකතු කරනවා.","Signature-based detection දන්නා attack patterns සොයනවා; anomaly-based detection සාමාන්‍ය behavior එකෙන් වෙනස් දේ සොයනවා. Alarm එකක් තිබුණා කියලා attack එකක් අනිවාර්යයෙන්ම නැහැ. Actual attack/normal කියන තත්ත්වය සහ alarm/no alarm කියන තීරණය වෙන් කර TP, FP, TN, FN හඳුනාගන්න."],"definition":{"term":"Detection and monitoring","text":"IDS detects and alerts; IPS can actively prevent detected malicious traffic; SIEM aggregates and correlates security events; UTM combines multiple gateway security functions."},"diagram":"detection","table":{"headers":["Actual condition","Alarm","No alarm"],"rows":[["Actual attack","True Positive (TP)","False Negative (FN)"],["Normal activity","False Positive (FP)","True Negative (TN)"]]},"bullets":[{"en":"Signature-based detection","si":"Known malicious patterns සමඟ සසඳනවා; හඳුනාගත් patterns සඳහා හොඳයි, නමුත් signatures update කළ යුතුයි."},{"en":"Anomaly-based detection","si":"Defined/learned normal behavior එකෙන් වෙනස් දේ සොයනවා; අලුත් හැසිරීම් හඳුනාගත හැකි නමුත් false alarms ඇති විය හැකියි."},{"en":"UTM versus SIEM","si":"UTM = එකට එකතු කළ security controls. SIEM = විවිධ sources වල logs සහ events සම්බන්ධ කර බලන monitoring."},{"en":"IDS versus IPS","si":"IDS එක alert දීම මූලිකයි; IPS එක detection එකට අමතරව traffic නවත්වන්න පුළුවන්."}],"example":{"q":"An IDS raises an intrusion alarm when a student legitimately downloads lecture slides. Classify the result.","steps":["Actual condition: normal, legitimate activity.","Detector decision: alarm/positive.","Normal activity + alarm gives a False Positive."],"answer":"False Positive (FP): a false alarm on legitimate activity. A real attack that produces no alarm would instead be a False Negative.","si":"“Positive” කියන්නේ alarm එකක් දුන්නා කියන එකයි. “False” කියන්නේ එම alarm තීරණය වැරදියි. ඒ නිසා legitimate download එකක් සඳහා alarm = FP."},"trap":{"en":"False positive and false negative are not interchangeable.","si":"FP = අනිසි alarm. FN = හඳුනා නොගත් සැබෑ attack එක."}},{"id":"vpn","title":"12.6 VPN and tunnelling: define the protection boundary","pages":[26,27],"si":["Colombo office එකේ data Kandy office එකට public Internet හරහා යවනවා කියලා හිතන්න. නිසි ලෙස සකස් කළ VPN එක gateways හෝ endpoints අතර protected logical tunnel එකක් ලබාදෙන්න පුළුවන්. Tunnelling කියන්නේ මුල් packet එක තවත් protocol packet එකක් තුළ encapsulate කර යැවීමයි.","Tunnel එකට පිටතින් දත්ත ආරක්ෂාව අවසන් විය හැකි තැන ගැනත් හිතන්න. VPN gateway එකෙන් පසු internal network එකට ගිය traffic, compromised laptop එකක්, හෝ vulnerable application එකක් VPN එක පමණක් හදා දෙන්නේ නැහැ. Processing සහ encapsulation overhead නිසා performance/capacity එකත් සලකා බලන්න."],"definition":{"term":"VPN and tunnelling","text":"A VPN provides a protected logical connection across shared or untrusted networks. Tunnelling encapsulates original traffic inside an outer protocol for transport."},"diagram":"vpn","table":{"headers":["Benefit","Limitation"],"rows":[["Protect traffic between configured VPN endpoints","Protection may end at the gateway"],["Support site-to-site and remote access","A compromised endpoint can still misuse access"],["Can protect confidentiality and integrity with appropriate configuration","Additional processing and encapsulation overhead"],["Carry traffic across a shared network","Does not repair application vulnerabilities or guarantee anonymity"]]},"example":{"q":"Two offices need to exchange sensitive business traffic across the public Internet. Propose a solution and one remaining requirement.","steps":["Use a suitable authenticated, encrypted site-to-site VPN between controlled gateways.","Restrict traffic allowed through the tunnel to required services.","Continue protecting endpoints and applications; identify where tunnel protection ends."],"answer":"A properly configured site-to-site VPN can protect traffic across the public network. Endpoint hardening, authorization, application security and monitoring remain necessary beyond the tunnel itself.","si":"VPN එක channel එක ආරක්ෂා කරයි; channel එක භාවිත කරන සෑම user/program එකක්ම ආරක්ෂිතයි කියා සහතික නොකරයි."},"trap":{"en":"Encapsulation alone is not encryption, and a VPN is not complete endpoint security.","si":"Packet එක වෙනත් packet එකක් තුළ දැමීම පමණක් රහස්‍යභාවය ලබාදෙන්නේ නැහැ; නිවැරදි cryptographic protection සහ configuration අවශ්‍යයි."}}],"checkpoint":[{"q":"Which rule protects the firewall itself?","a":"The Stealth Rule restricts unauthorized traffic directed to the firewall.","si":"Firewall එක හරහා යන traffic සහ firewall එකටම යන traffic වෙන් කර බලන්න."},{"q":"Which rule denies otherwise unmatched traffic?","a":"The Cleanup / default-deny rule.","si":"කලින් allow නොකළ packet එක අවසානයේ deny කරනවා."},{"q":"Which HTTP and SMTP ports are used in the lecture?","a":"HTTP: TCP 80. SMTP: TCP 25.","si":"මෙය lecture examples වල ports; protocol එකත් සමඟ ලියන්න."},{"q":"Which firewall technique tracks active connections?","a":"Stateful Packet Inspection.","si":"Packet එක tracked authorized connection එකකට ගැළපෙනවාද කියා බලනවා."},{"q":"What is a False Negative?","a":"An actual attack that is not detected and produces no alarm.","si":"Attack එකක් තිබුණත් detector එක මඟහැරියා නම් FN."}],"summary":"Packet එක trace කරන විට source/destination, ports, protocol සහ direction ලියන්න. First match ලැබුණාම නවතින්න. Stealth = firewall එකම ආරක්ෂා කිරීම; Cleanup = unmatched traffic deny කිරීම. Stateful inspection, DMZ, IDS/IPS, SIEM සහ VPN එකිනෙකට වෙනස් layers බවත් ඒවායේ සීමා තිබෙන බවත් scenario එකට සම්බන්ධ කර පැහැදිලි කරන්න."}],"clinic":[{"id":"clinic-matrix","title":"Build an access matrix","week":9,"pages":[29],"q":"At a university, U1 (Professor) may Read all resources. U2 (Graduate Student) may Read Course Materials and Department Email. U3 (Staff) may Read Course Materials and Write Research Datasets. U4 (Guest) has no access. Build an access matrix.","steps":["Create subject rows U1–U4 and object columns R1 Course Materials, R2 Research Datasets, R3 Department Email, R4 Lab Computers.","Enter only the rights explicitly granted by the prompt.","Use — for denied or unspecified rights."],"answer":"| User | R1 Course | R2 Research | R3 Email | R4 Lab |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| U1 Professor | R | R | R | R |\n| U2 Graduate | R | — | R | — |\n| U3 Staff | R | W | — | — |\n| U4 Guest | — | — | — | — |","si":"Users පේළිවලත් resources තීරුවලත් දාන්න. U3ට Research සඳහා W පමණක් දුන් නිසා R අනුමාන කර එකතු නොකරන්න. Guestට කිසිදු permission එකක් නොදීමෙන් default-deny පදනම පැහැදිලි වේ."},{"id":"clinic-models","title":"Choose DAC, MAC or RBAC","week":9,"pages":[29],"q":"Select DAC, MAC or RBAC for (a) hospital job duties, (b) a classified government laboratory, and (c) a collaborative document with owner-managed sharing.","steps":["Hospital decisions depend on job functions.","The classified lab uses security labels and clearances.","The document owner chooses who receives viewing or editing rights."],"answer":"(a) RBAC. (b) MAC. (c) DAC. State the decision basis for each choice, rather than naming the model alone.","si":"Role අනුව නම් RBAC, classification/clearance අනුව නම් MAC, ownerගේ අවසර බෙදාදීම අනුව නම් DAC ලෙස හඳුනාගන්න. එකම system එකකට models කිහිපයක් එකට තිබිය හැකියි."},{"id":"clinic-sso","title":"Evaluate a university SSO proposal","week":10,"pages":[30],"q":"A university wants one login for the LMS, library, computer labs and help desk. Give two benefits, two risks and explain why MFA matters.","steps":["Identify benefits from fewer repeated sign-ins and central administration.","Consider both compromise and unavailability of the central identity service.","Connect MFA to the wider impact of a stolen central password."],"answer":"Benefits: reduced sign-in/password burden and centralized account administration. Risks: central account compromise can expose several services; identity-provider outage can block access. Use distinct-factor MFA, secure sessions, monitor identity events and make the identity service resilient.","si":"SSO පහසුකමෙන් logins අඩු වෙනවා සහ accounts පාලනය පහසු වෙනවා. නමුත් central account එක කඩාවැටුණොත් සේවා ගොඩකට බලපාන නිසා MFA සහ central service එකේ resilience වැදගත් වේ."},{"id":"clinic-challenge","title":"Explain replay-resistant authentication","week":10,"pages":[30],"q":"Explain a challenge–response authentication sequence using a fresh nonce to defend against replay.","steps":["Client presents the account identifier.","Server creates a fresh unpredictable nonce.","Client computes a secret-dependent response bound to that nonce.","Server verifies the response for the current challenge before creating an authenticated session."],"answer":"A previously recorded response is tied to an old challenge and should fail for a new nonce. Keep authentication secrets protected, use a sound protocol and protected transport, and do not treat freshness as a solution to every authentication attack.","si":"අලුත් nonce එකට අලුත් response එකක් අවශ්‍යයි. එම නිසා පරණ response එක නැවත යැවීම ගැළපෙන්නේ නැහැ. Nonce එක පමණක් තිබීමෙන් protocol එකේ සෑම අවදානමක්ම ඉවත් වෙන්නේ නැහැ."},{"id":"clinic-salts","title":"Explain two benefits of unique salts","week":10,"pages":[30],"q":"State two benefits of unique random salts when storing password verifiers.","steps":["Different salts vary the input even when two users choose the same password.","A precomputed table for one salt is not reusable as a universal table for every account."],"answer":"Unique salts make identical passwords produce distinct stored verifiers and reduce cross-account reuse of precomputed hash tables. Salts are normally stored with verifiers and do not need to be secret; use a suitably slow password-hashing function as well.","si":"Salt එක password entropy එක වැඩි කරන රහස් password එකක් නොවේ. එකම password තිබුණත් verifier වෙනස් කර accounts අතර සරල comparison සහ precomputation reuse අඩු කිරීම එහි අරමුණයි."},{"id":"clinic-stealth","title":"Place a firewall-management protection rule","week":12,"pages":[30],"q":"A firewall needs a rule restricting direct traffic to its own management address. Name the rule and state where it usually appears.","steps":["Identify the protected destination as the firewall itself.","A first-match policy must process management protection before broad permits."],"answer":"Use a Stealth Rule near the beginning of the rule list, before broad general allow rules. If approved administration is necessary, use a narrowly scoped trusted-management exception before the deny; do not block legitimate management unintentionally.","si":"Firewall එක හරහා යන traffic සහ firewall එකටම යන traffic වෙනස්. Management IP එකට අනවශ්‍ය ප්‍රවේශය broad allow එකකින් ලැබීමට පෙර නවත්වන්න."},{"id":"clinic-firewall","title":"Construct a simplified stateless ACL","week":12,"pages":[31],"q":"Protect 192.168.10.0/24. Block internal HTTP requests to 100.23.13.11; allow other outgoing TCP 80; allow external HTTP to web server 192.168.10.123; deny remaining traffic. Construct core stateless rules.","steps":["Place the blocked-destination deny before the general HTTP allow.","Allow internal requests to TCP destination port 80.","Include the source-port-80 return pattern used in the guide’s simplified stateless model.","Allow incoming HTTP to the web server and its response traffic.","Finish with a catch-all deny."],"answer":"| Order | Source | S.Port | Destination | D.Port | Protocol | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 192.168.10.0/24 | Any | 100.23.13.11 | Any | Any | Deny |\n| 2 | 192.168.10.0/24 | Any | Any | 80 | TCP | Allow |\n| 3 | Any | 80 | 192.168.10.0/24 | Any | TCP | Allow |\n| 4 | Any | Any | 192.168.10.123 | 80 | TCP | Allow |\n| 5 | 192.168.10.123 | 80 | Any | Any | TCP | Allow |\n| 6 | Any | Any | Any | Any | Any | Deny |\n\nGuide-model caveat: rule 1 blocks all traffic to that destination, which is broader than blocking HTTP alone. The table follows the PDF. Source port 80 alone does not prove a valid reply; directions, interfaces, state tracking, anti-spoofing and approved management must be considered in a real policy.","si":"විශේෂ deny එක general allow එකට කලින් තිබිය යුතුයි. මේ PDF table එකේ පළමු rule එක HTTP පමණක් නොව එම destination එකට සියලු traffic deny කරන බවත් බලන්න. Reply කියා හඳුනාගැනීමට source port 80 පමණක් ප්‍රමාණවත් නැති නිසා මෙය lecture-level stateless උදාහරණයක් ලෙස ඉගෙනගන්න."},{"id":"clinic-sites","title":"Compare a cold site with alternatives","week":11,"pages":[31],"q":"A medium-sized company has severe budget limits and chooses a Cold Site with backups. Explain Cold Site and suggest two alternatives.","steps":["A cold site provides premises and basic infrastructure but requires equipment and setup after a disruption.","Compare a warm site’s partial readiness with a hot site’s higher readiness.","Connect the selection to acceptable downtime, data recovery needs and budget."],"answer":"Cold Site: lower ongoing cost but longer preparation/restoration time. Warm Site: some equipment/configuration already available, with further setup and data restoration required. Hot Site: prepared compatible infrastructure for quicker recovery, usually at greater ongoing cost. Backups and tested recovery procedures remain necessary.","si":"Cold site එක අඩු වියදම් වුණත් disaster එකෙන් පසු වැඩි සකස් කිරීමක් අවශ්‍යයි. Warm සහ Hot සූදානම්භාවයෙන් වෙනස් වන නිසා ව්‍යාපාරයට දරාගත හැකි downtime සහ budget අනුව තෝරන්න."},{"id":"clinic-provider","title":"Evaluate a third-party DR provider","week":11,"pages":[32],"q":"Name two factors to evaluate before contracting a third-party disaster-recovery provider and explain why.","steps":["Choose a practical capacity factor based on the required workload.","Choose a support or expertise factor needed during failover."],"answer":"1. Sufficient redundant equipment and network capacity to support the organization’s real transaction volume during failover. 2. Skilled personnel and reliable vendor support to execute and troubleshoot recovery within the required service objectives. Verify these through tests and contractual commitments rather than relying on advertised capacity alone.","si":"Server ඉඩ තිබෙනවාද කියන එක පමණක් නොව සැබෑ workload එක run කළ හැකිද බලන්න. Disaster වෙලාවේ recovery කිරීමට දැනුම ඇති අය සහ support ලබාගත හැකිද යන්නත් පරීක්ෂා කළ යුතුයි."}],"mock":[{"id":"guide-p1-01","week":9,"part":1,"topic":"Access control","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":33,"answerPage":40,"si":"Access request එක කරන user හෝ process එක Subject වේ. File එක වැනි ආරක්ෂා කරන දේ Object එකයි.","rationale":"A subject is the user or process requesting access to a protected object.","format":"single","q":"Which term identifies an entity that requests access to a protected object?","options":["Firewall","Subject","Salt","Certificate"],"correct":[1],"answer":"Subject. A subject is the user or process requesting access to a protected object."},{"id":"guide-p1-02","week":9,"part":1,"topic":"Access control","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":33,"answerPage":40,"si":"මෙහි අවසර තීරණය වන්නේ Doctor කියන job role එක අනුවයි. ඒ නිසා මෙය RBAC වන අතර එක් එක් userට වෙන වෙනම permission දීම ප්‍රධාන පදනම නොවේ.","rationale":"RBAC associates permissions with organizational roles and assigns those roles to users.","format":"single","q":"A doctor receives permissions through the Doctor role. Which policy is used?","options":["DAC","MAC","RBAC","Default Allow"],"correct":[2],"answer":"RBAC. RBAC associates permissions with organizational roles and assigns those roles to users."},{"id":"guide-p1-03","week":9,"part":1,"topic":"Access control","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":33,"answerPage":40,"si":"Classification label එක සහ userගේ clearance එක පද්ධතියේ නීතියට අනුව සසඳන නිසා MAC යොදාගනී. Ownerගේ කැමැත්තෙන් එම නීතිය මඟහැරිය නොහැකියි.","rationale":"Mandatory Access Control enforces classifications, clearances and the applicable central policy.","format":"single","q":"A government research lab assigns security classification labels and clearances. Choose the model.","options":["MAC","DAC","Password Policy","ACL only"],"correct":[0],"answer":"MAC. Mandatory Access Control enforces classifications, clearances and the applicable central policy."},{"id":"guide-p1-04","week":9,"part":1,"topic":"Access control","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":33,"answerPage":40,"si":"File owner තමන්ගේ resource එක share කරන අය තෝරන නිසා DAC ගැළපේ. මෙය role එක හෝ military classification එක මත පමණක් ගන්නා තීරණයක් නොවේ.","rationale":"DAC allows an authorized owner discretion over sharing a resource.","format":"single","q":"A file owner allows another user to edit a document. Which is the best model?","options":["RBAC","DAC","IDS","Mandatory clearance"],"correct":[1],"answer":"DAC. DAC allows an authorized owner discretion over sharing a resource."},{"id":"guide-p1-05","week":9,"part":1,"topic":"Access control","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":34,"answerPage":40,"si":"එක් file එකකට කාට මොන අවසර තිබේද කියා බලන්න එම file එකේ ACL එක බලන්න. මෙය object එක වටා සංවිධානය කළ ලැයිස්තුවකි.","rationale":"An object-associated ACL lists the subjects and rights for that particular file.","format":"single","q":"Which representation tells you who can read a particular file?","options":["A file ACL","A user password","A nonce","An RPO"],"correct":[0],"answer":"A file ACL. An object-associated ACL lists the subjects and rights for that particular file."},{"id":"guide-p1-06","week":9,"part":1,"topic":"Access control","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":34,"answerPage":40,"si":"Capability එකෙන් holderට resource එකක නිශ්චිත වැඩක් කිරීමට බලය ලැබේ. ඒ නිසා එය forge කිරීම සහ සොරකම් කිරීම වළක්වා ආරක්ෂා කළ යුතුයි.","rationale":"A capability conveys specific authority over a resource and must resist forgery and theft.","format":"single","q":"A user holds an unforgeable reference allowing Write on Object A. This is a:","options":["Salt","Capability","Firewall","SSO session only"],"correct":[1],"answer":"Capability. A capability conveys specific authority over a resource and must resist forgery and theft."},{"id":"guide-p1-07","week":9,"part":1,"topic":"Access control","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":34,"answerPage":40,"si":"Login වීමෙන් identity එක තහවුරු වුවත් සියලු resources සඳහා අවසර ලැබෙන්නේ නැහැ. එක් එක් operation එකට authorization වෙනම පරීක්ෂා කළ යුතුයි.","rationale":"Authentication verifies identity; authorization separately determines which resources and operations are allowed.","format":"single","q":"A user with successful authentication must be permitted to access every resource.","options":["True","False"],"correct":[1],"answer":"False. Authentication verifies identity; authorization separately determines which resources and operations are allowed."},{"id":"guide-p1-08","week":9,"part":1,"topic":"Access control","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":34,"answerPage":40,"si":"Payment එක හදන අය සහ approve කරන අය වෙන් කිරීම Separation of Duty වේ. එකම sensitive action එකකට දෙදෙනෙකු එක්ව සහභාගී වීම Dual Control ලෙස වෙනම හඳුනාගන්න.","rationale":"Separation of Duty assigns different critical workflow steps to different people.","format":"single","q":"A clerk creates a payment and a different clerk approves it. Identify the principle.","options":["Dual Control only","Separation of Duty","Default Allow","Replay"],"correct":[1],"answer":"Separation of Duty. Separation of Duty assigns different critical workflow steps to different people."},{"id":"guide-p1-09","week":9,"part":1,"topic":"Access control","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":34,"answerPage":40,"si":"Closed Policy එකේ සාමාන්‍ය තීරණය Deny යන්නයි. පැහැදිලිව අවසර දුන් rule එකක් තිබුණොත් පමණක් access ලබා දෙයි.","rationale":"A closed policy denies a request unless an applicable permission explicitly allows it.","format":"blank","q":"What is the default decision of a Closed Access Control Policy?","accepted":["deny","default deny","deny access","deny by default"],"answer":"Deny. A closed policy denies a request unless an applicable permission explicitly allows it."},{"id":"guide-p1-10","week":10,"part":1,"topic":"User authentication","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":34,"answerPage":40,"si":"Username එකෙන් user තමන් කවුද කියා කියනවා. එය හරිද කියා password හෝ වෙනත් proof එකක් පරීක්ෂා කිරීම verification වේ.","rationale":"Entering a username presents an identity claim; checking the authentication proof comes later.","format":"single","q":"A username is entered before a password is checked. Username entry is:","options":["Authorization","Identification","Recovery","Mirroring"],"correct":[1],"answer":"Identification. Entering a username presents an identity claim; checking the authentication proof comes later."},{"id":"guide-p1-11","week":10,"part":1,"topic":"User authentication","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":34,"answerPage":40,"si":"Password එක දන්නා දෙයක් වන අතර token එක සතු දෙයක් වේ. වෙනස් factor categories දෙකක් ඇති නිසා මෙය MFA සඳහා සුදුසු උදාහරණයකි.","rationale":"A password is a knowledge factor and a security token is a possession factor.","format":"single","q":"Which pairing represents different authentication factor categories?","options":["Password + PIN","PIN + Security question","Password + Security token","Two passwords"],"correct":[2],"answer":"Password + Security token. A password is a knowledge factor and a security token is a possession factor."},{"id":"guide-p1-12","week":10,"part":1,"topic":"User authentication","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":35,"answerPage":41,"si":"මෙහි attacker login page එකට requests යවන්නේ නැහැ. සොරකම් කළ hashes තමන්ගේ පරිගණකයේ අනුමාන සමඟ සසඳන නිසා Offline Dictionary attack වේ.","rationale":"Offline guessing operates locally on stolen password verifiers rather than submitting guesses to the live login service.","format":"single","q":"Stolen password hashes are tested without using the login page. Identify the attack.","options":["Replay","Offline Dictionary","Workstation Hijacking","SYN Flood"],"correct":[1],"answer":"Offline Dictionary. Offline guessing operates locally on stolen password verifiers rather than submitting guesses to the live login service."},{"id":"guide-p1-13","week":10,"part":1,"topic":"User authentication","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":35,"answerPage":41,"si":"එකම ජනප්‍රිය password එක accounts ගොඩකට අත්හදා බැලීම password spraying වේ. එක් account එකකට guesses ගොඩක් යැවීමෙන් මෙය වෙනස් වේ.","rationale":"Password spraying applies one or a few common candidate passwords across many accounts.","format":"single","q":"A common password is tested across hundreds of accounts. Which attack fits?","options":["Popular Password Attack","Collision Attack","MAC Spoofing","Packet Filtering"],"correct":[0],"answer":"Popular Password Attack. Password spraying applies one or a few common candidate passwords across many accounts."},{"id":"guide-p1-14","week":10,"part":1,"topic":"User authentication","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":35,"answerPage":41,"si":"එකම password එකට වෙනස් salt දුන්නාම hashing input වෙනස් වේ. එම නිසා stored verifier එකත් වෙනස් විය හැකි අතර accounts අතර සරල hash comparison අඩු කරයි.","rationale":"Different salts vary the input to password hashing, so the same password need not produce the same stored verifier.","format":"single","q":"Different random salts can make identical passwords produce distinct stored verifiers.","options":["True","False"],"correct":[0],"answer":"True. Different salts vary the input to password hashing, so the same password need not produce the same stored verifier."},{"id":"guide-p1-15","week":10,"part":1,"topic":"User authentication","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":35,"answerPage":41,"si":"පරණ response එක පරණ nonce එකට සම්බන්ධයි. අලුත් challenge එකක් දුන්නාම පරණ response එක නැවත යැවීම ගැළපෙන්නේ නැහැ.","rationale":"A fresh nonce binds the expected response to the current authentication exchange.","format":"single","q":"What helps limit replay of captured challenge-response credentials?","options":["Reused nonce","Fresh nonce","Longer username","Shared browser"],"correct":[1],"answer":"Fresh nonce. A fresh nonce binds the expected response to the current authentication exchange."},{"id":"guide-p1-16","week":10,"part":1,"topic":"User authentication","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":35,"answerPage":41,"si":"එක් central login එකකින් සම්බන්ධ සේවා කිහිපයකට යෑම SSO වේ. ඒ පහසුව සමඟ central account එකේ ආරක්ෂාවත් වැදගත් වේ.","rationale":"Single Sign-On supports one central authentication arrangement for several associated applications.","format":"single","q":"A university uses one central login for Library, LMS and Student Portal. This is:","options":["RAID","SSO","DAC","UTM"],"correct":[1],"answer":"SSO. Single Sign-On supports one central authentication arrangement for several associated applications."},{"id":"guide-p1-17","week":10,"part":1,"topic":"User authentication","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":35,"answerPage":41,"si":"Fingerprint හෝ face වැනි ශරීර ලක්ෂණයක් ද, typing rhythm වැනි හැසිරීමේ ලක්ෂණයක් ද මෙහි ගත හැකියි. Password එක biometric එකක් නොවේ.","rationale":"Physical or behavioural biometrics include a fingerprint, face, retina, typing rhythm, voice pattern or handwriting dynamics.","format":"blank","q":"Name one physical or behavioral biometric from the uploaded lecture.","accepted":["fingerprint","face","facial recognition","retina","retinal pattern","iris","typing rhythm","keystroke dynamics","voice pattern","handwriting","handwriting dynamics"],"answer":"Any valid example: fingerprint, face, retina, typing rhythm, voice pattern or handwriting dynamics. Physical or behavioural biometrics include a fingerprint, face, retina, typing rhythm, voice pattern or handwriting dynamics."},{"id":"guide-p1-18","week":10,"part":1,"topic":"User authentication","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":35,"answerPage":41,"si":"User දැනටමත් login වී workstation එක හැර ගියොත් වෙන කෙනෙකුට එම session එක භාවිත කළ හැකියි. ඒ සඳහා password එක දැනගැනීම අනිවාර්ය නැහැ.","rationale":"An already-authenticated unattended session may be abused without knowing the user’s password.","format":"single","q":"Workstation hijacking necessarily requires an attacker to know the user's password.","options":["True","False"],"correct":[1],"answer":"False. An already-authenticated unattended session may be abused without knowing the user’s password."},{"id":"guide-p1-19","week":11,"part":1,"topic":"Disaster recovery and continuity","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":35,"answerPage":41,"si":"බිඳ වැටුණු database එක නැවත ගොඩනැගීම DR කාර්යයකි. සේවාව තාවකාලිකව දිගටම කරගෙන යෑම BC කාර්යයකි.","rationale":"Disaster Recovery restores disrupted systems, data and infrastructure.","format":"single","q":"Rebuilding a failed primary database after a disaster is mainly:","options":["Business Continuity","Disaster Recovery","Authentication","RBAC"],"correct":[1],"answer":"Disaster Recovery. Disaster Recovery restores disrupted systems, data and infrastructure."},{"id":"guide-p1-20","week":11,"part":1,"topic":"Disaster recovery and continuity","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":36,"answerPage":41,"si":"Disaster එක තිබියදීත් essential business වැඩ තාවකාලික site එකෙන් පවත්වා ගැනීම BCP අරමුණයි. මුල් පද්ධතිය නැවත හදන DR වැඩත් සමඟ මෙය එකට ක්‍රියා කරයි.","rationale":"Business Continuity maintains essential business operations while disruption is ongoing.","format":"single","q":"Continuing essential customer operations at a temporary site is mainly:","options":["BCP","Hashing","DAC","Authentication"],"correct":[0],"answer":"BCP. Business Continuity maintains essential business operations while disruption is ongoing."},{"id":"guide-p1-21","week":11,"part":1,"topic":"Disaster recovery and continuity","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":36,"answerPage":41,"si":"Cold Site එකේ තැන සහ මූලික පහසුකම් තිබුණත් පද්ධති සූදානම් කිරීමේ වැඩ ඉතිරි වෙයි. ඒ නිසා Hot හෝ Mirrored site එකකට වඩා සාමාන්‍යයෙන් කාලය වැඩි වේ.","rationale":"A cold site has basic facilities and typically requires equipment installation or preparation before operation.","format":"single","q":"Which site generally has basic facilities but requires more installation before operation?","options":["Mirrored","Hot","Cold","Fully active dual data center"],"correct":[2],"answer":"Cold. A cold site has basic facilities and typically requires equipment installation or preparation before operation."},{"id":"guide-p1-22","week":11,"part":1,"topic":"Disaster recovery and continuity","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":36,"answerPage":41,"si":"Mirrored Site එක ප්‍රධාන site එකට සමීපව සමාන infrastructure සහ data copy එකක් පවත්වා ගනී. එය ඉක්මන් recovery සඳහා උදව් වන නමුත් independent backups වෙනුවට ප්‍රමාණවත් නොවේ.","rationale":"A mirrored site closely duplicates infrastructure and replicates data for high readiness; actual recovery still depends on design.","format":"single","q":"An alternate site closely replicates the primary data center for very rapid recovery. This is:","options":["Cold Site","Mirrored Site","Mutual Backup","Password Vault"],"correct":[1],"answer":"Mirrored Site. A mirrored site closely duplicates infrastructure and replicates data for high readiness; actual recovery still depends on design."},{"id":"guide-p1-23","week":11,"part":1,"topic":"Disaster recovery and continuity","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":36,"answerPage":41,"si":"SDO කියන්නේ Service Delivery Objective යන්නයි. එය Alternate Mode එකේ ලබාදීමට බලාපොරොත්තු වන සේවා මට්ටම පෙන්වයි.","rationale":"Service Delivery Objective describes the target service level while operating in Alternate Mode.","format":"blank","q":"What does SDO mean in the disaster-recovery lecture?","accepted":["service delivery objective"],"answer":"Service Delivery Objective. Service Delivery Objective describes the target service level while operating in Alternate Mode."},{"id":"guide-p1-24","week":11,"part":1,"topic":"Disaster recovery and continuity","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":36,"answerPage":41,"si":"Simulated outage එකක් යොදා plan එක වැඩ කරනවාද කියා බලන්නේ Testing අදියරේදීයි. අඩුපාඩු හඳුනාගෙන පසුව plan එක වැඩිදියුණු කරයි.","rationale":"Testing exercises the planned procedures and evaluates whether the recovery arrangement works.","format":"single","q":"A company exercises its continuity plan in a simulated outage. Which BCP phase?","options":["Maintenance","Testing","Project Initiation","Design"],"correct":[1],"answer":"Testing. Testing exercises the planned procedures and evaluates whether the recovery arrangement works."},{"id":"guide-p1-25","week":11,"part":1,"topic":"Disaster recovery and continuity","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":36,"answerPage":41,"si":"RAID එක disk failure වැනි අවස්ථා සඳහා redundancy දෙනවා. නමුත් flood, ransomware, වැරදි deletion හෝ මුළු site එකේ හානිය සඳහා එය තනිව backup එකක් නොවේ.","rationale":"Local disk redundancy does not protect against all deletion, corruption, ransomware or site-wide destruction.","format":"single","q":"RAID alone guarantees full protection against flood and ransomware incidents.","options":["True","False"],"correct":[1],"answer":"False. Local disk redundancy does not protect against all deletion, corruption, ransomware or site-wide destruction."},{"id":"guide-p1-26","week":11,"part":1,"topic":"Disaster recovery and continuity","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":36,"answerPage":42,"si":"සමාගම් දෙකක් එකිනෙකාට recovery facilities ලබාදීමට එකඟ වීම Mutual Backup වේ. Compatibility සහ එකවර දෙපාර්ශ්වයට disaster එක බලපාන අවදානමත් සලකා බැලිය යුතුයි.","rationale":"Mutual Backup is a reciprocal arrangement between compatible organizations to provide recovery facilities.","format":"single","q":"Two compatible companies agree to provide recovery facilities for each other. Identify the approach.","options":["Remote Journaling","Mutual Backup","Hashing","VPN"],"correct":[1],"answer":"Mutual Backup. Mutual Backup is a reciprocal arrangement between compatible organizations to provide recovery facilities."},{"id":"guide-p1-27","week":12,"part":1,"topic":"Network security","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":37,"answerPage":42,"si":"කලින් rules කිසිවකට නොගැළපුණු traffic අවසාන cleanup rule එකෙන් deny කරයි. First-match ACL එකක එය සාමාන්‍යයෙන් අවසානයේ තබයි.","rationale":"The cleanup/default-deny rule rejects otherwise unmatched traffic at the end of the first-match ACL.","format":"single","q":"Which firewall rule usually denies unmatched traffic at the end of an ACL?","options":["Stealth","Cleanup","Authentication","NAT"],"correct":[1],"answer":"Cleanup. The cleanup/default-deny rule rejects otherwise unmatched traffic at the end of the first-match ACL."},{"id":"guide-p1-28","week":12,"part":1,"topic":"Network security","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":37,"answerPage":42,"si":"මෙහි ආරක්ෂා කරන්නේ firewall එකමයි. Broad allow rulesවලට පෙර management address එකට අනවසර traffic නවත්වන rule එක වැදගත් වේ.","rationale":"A stealth rule protects traffic directed at the firewall’s own interfaces or management address.","format":"single","q":"Which rule helps prevent unauthorized traffic directed to the firewall itself?","options":["Stealth Rule","Cleanup only","Allow All","Mirroring"],"correct":[0],"answer":"Stealth Rule. A stealth rule protects traffic directed at the firewall’s own interfaces or management address."},{"id":"guide-p1-29","week":12,"part":1,"topic":"Network security","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":37,"answerPage":42,"si":"මෙම lecture උදාහරණයේ HTTP සඳහා TCP 80 යොදාගනී. Port අංකය සහ protocol එක දෙකම නිවැරදිව හඳුනාගන්න.","rationale":"The lecture’s HTTP example uses TCP destination port 80; SMTP uses TCP 25.","format":"single","q":"Which packet attribute identifies TCP web service in the lecture?","options":["TCP 22","TCP 25","TCP 80","UDP 123"],"correct":[2],"answer":"TCP 80. The lecture’s HTTP example uses TCP destination port 80; SMTP uses TCP 25."},{"id":"guide-p1-30","week":12,"part":1,"topic":"Network security","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":37,"answerPage":42,"si":"Stateful firewall එක connection එකේ තත්ත්වය මතක තබාගනී. Packet එක allowed session එකකට අදාළද කියාත් පරීක්ෂා කිරීම එහි වෙනසයි.","rationale":"Stateful Packet Inspection tracks authorized session state and checks packets against that context.","format":"single","q":"Which filtering technique maintains information about an authorized TCP session?","options":["Stateless","Stateful Packet Inspection","Simple XOR","HMAC"],"correct":[1],"answer":"Stateful Packet Inspection. Stateful Packet Inspection tracks authorized session state and checks packets against that context."},{"id":"guide-p1-31","week":12,"part":1,"topic":"Network security","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":37,"answerPage":42,"si":"Public server එකට Internet access අවශ්‍ය නමුත් confidential database එක direct exposure නොවිය යුතුයි. ඒ නිසා public server එක DMZ එකක වෙන් කර inner access සීමා කරයි.","rationale":"A DMZ separates Internet-facing services from sensitive internal network resources.","format":"single","q":"Where should an Internet-facing public server be isolated from a confidential database?","options":["Only inside database subnet","DMZ","Password table","Certificate store"],"correct":[1],"answer":"DMZ. A DMZ separates Internet-facing services from sensitive internal network resources."},{"id":"guide-p1-32","week":12,"part":1,"topic":"Network security","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":37,"answerPage":42,"si":"Attack එකක් සිදුවී alarm නැත්නම් False Negative වේ. සාමාන්‍ය traffic එකකට alarm දුන්නොත් False Positive බව වෙනම මතක තබාගන්න.","rationale":"An actual attack with no alarm is a false negative. A false positive is an alarm on legitimate activity.","format":"single","q":"An IDS false positive means a real attack occurred but no alarm was raised.","options":["True","False"],"correct":[1],"answer":"False. An actual attack with no alarm is a false negative. A false positive is an alarm on legitimate activity."},{"id":"guide-p1-33","week":12,"part":1,"topic":"Network security","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":37,"answerPage":42,"si":"Firewall, server සහ application logs එකතු කර සම්බන්ධ කර බලන්නේ SIEM එකයි. මෙය single firewall rule එකක් හෝ backup site එකක් නොවේ.","rationale":"SIEM collects and correlates events from multiple security and system sources.","format":"single","q":"Which system primarily correlates firewall, server, and application security logs?","options":["SIEM","RAID","DAC","Cold Site"],"correct":[0],"answer":"SIEM. SIEM collects and correlates events from multiple security and system sources."},{"id":"guide-p1-34","week":12,"part":1,"topic":"Network security","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":38,"answerPage":42,"si":"IDS එක detect කර alert දෙන අතර IPS එකට blocking වැනි prevention action ගත හැකියි. එයින් සියලු attacks නවතිනවා කියා අදහස් නොවේ.","rationale":"An IPS can take preventive action such as blocking or interrupting detected malicious traffic.","format":"single","q":"Which technology can automatically block detected malicious network traffic?","options":["IDS only","IPS","Password Salt","BCP"],"correct":[1],"answer":"IPS. An IPS can take preventive action such as blocking or interrupting detected malicious traffic."},{"id":"guide-p1-35","week":12,"part":1,"topic":"Network security","difficulty":"foundation","marks":1,"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":38,"answerPage":42,"si":"VPN කියන්නේ Virtual Private Network යන්නයි. Public network එකක් හරහා protected tunnel එකක් ලබාදෙන නමුත් compromised endpoint එකක් තනිව නිවැරදි කරන්නේ නැහැ.","rationale":"A Virtual Private Network creates a protected logical connection across a public or shared network.","format":"blank","q":"What does VPN stand for?","accepted":["virtual private network"],"answer":"Virtual Private Network. A Virtual Private Network creates a protected logical connection across a public or shared network."},{"id":"guide-p2-01","week":9,"part":2,"format":"structured","topic":"Guide structured practice","difficulty":"applied","marks":4,"q":"Construct a 3×3 Access Matrix for: Student may Read Own Results and Course Notes; Lecturer may Read/Write Assigned Results and Course Notes; Administrator may Manage Accounts only. Use — for denied rights.","answer":"Rows = subjects; columns = objects.\n\n| Subject | Results | Course Notes | Accounts |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Student | R (own) | R | — |\n| Lecturer | R/W (assigned) | R/W | — |\n| Administrator | — | — | Manage |\n\nUnspecified rights are denied.","si":"මුලින් subjects පේළිවලත් resources තීරුවලත් දාන්න. ප්‍රශ්නයේ පැහැදිලිව දුන් rights පමණක් ඇතුළත් කර, අනෙක් තැන්වල no access දක්වන්න. Write තිබීමෙන් Readත් ලැබෙනවා කියා අනුමාන නොකරන්න.","rubric":[{"point":"Define clear subject rows and object columns.","marks":1},{"point":"Student: Results R (own), Notes R, Accounts —.","marks":1},{"point":"Lecturer: Results R/W (assigned), Notes R/W, Accounts —.","marks":1},{"point":"Admin: Results —, Notes —, Accounts Manage.","marks":1}],"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":38,"answerPage":42},{"id":"guide-p2-02","week":9,"part":2,"format":"structured","topic":"Guide structured practice","difficulty":"applied","marks":4,"q":"Explain DAC, MAC and RBAC by selecting the best policy for (a) owner-controlled file sharing, (b) classified defense documents, and (c) hospital job permissions.","answer":"1. DAC: owner/authorized entity determines sharing permissions.\n2. MAC: security classifications and clearances.\n3. RBAC: permissions linked to organizational roles.\n4. Correct application: (a) DAC, (b) MAC, (c) RBAC.","si":"Policy එක තෝරන විට අවසර තීරණය කරන පදනම බලන්න. Ownerගේ තීරණය DAC, label සහ clearance MAC, job role එක RBAC වේ. නමට අමතරව එය scenario එකට ගැළපෙන හේතුවත් කියන්න.","rubric":[{"point":"DAC: owner/authorized entity determines sharing permissions.","marks":1},{"point":"MAC: security classifications and clearances.","marks":1},{"point":"RBAC: permissions linked to organizational roles.","marks":1},{"point":"Correct application: (a) DAC, (b) MAC, (c) RBAC.","marks":1}],"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":38,"answerPage":43},{"id":"guide-p2-03","week":9,"part":2,"format":"structured","topic":"Guide structured practice","difficulty":"applied","marks":4,"q":"A bank separates payment creation from approval and requires two officers for unusually large transfers. Identify and distinguish the two security requirements.","answer":"1. Separation of Duty divides payment creation and approval.\n2. SoD reduces conflict of interest and fraud.\n3. Dual Control requires multiple authorized individuals for the high-value transfer .\n4. State the difference: separate steps versus joint participation in a sensitive action.","si":"වෙනස් workflow පියවර වෙනස් පුද්ගලයන්ට දීම SoD වේ. එකම විශාල transfer එකට දෙදෙනෙකු එක්ව approve කිරීම Dual Control වේ. දෙකේ වෙනස සෘජුව පැහැදිලි කරන්න.","rubric":[{"point":"Separation of Duty divides payment creation and approval.","marks":1},{"point":"SoD reduces conflict of interest and fraud.","marks":1},{"point":"Dual Control requires multiple authorized individuals for the high-value transfer .","marks":1},{"point":"State the difference: separate steps versus joint participation in a sensitive action.","marks":1}],"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":38,"answerPage":43},{"id":"guide-p2-04","week":10,"part":2,"format":"structured","topic":"Guide structured practice","difficulty":"applied","marks":4,"q":"Identify four authentication factor categories and give a valid example for each.","answer":"1. Know – Password or PIN.\n2. Have – Smart card/security token.\n3. Are – Fingerprint or face.\n4. Do – Typing rhythm or handwriting behavior .","si":"Factor category එක සහ එයට ගැළපෙන example එක යුගල වශයෙන් ලියන්න. Password සහ PIN දෙකම Know නිසා ඒ දෙක වෙනස් categories ලෙස නොලියන්න.","rubric":[{"point":"Know – Password or PIN.","marks":1},{"point":"Have – Smart card/security token.","marks":1},{"point":"Are – Fingerprint or face.","marks":1},{"point":"Do – Typing rhythm or handwriting behavior .","marks":1}],"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":38,"answerPage":43},{"id":"guide-p2-05","week":10,"part":2,"format":"structured","topic":"Guide structured practice","difficulty":"applied","marks":4,"q":"Explain password registration and login verification using a unique random salt and slow password hashing.","answer":"1. Registration: generate unique random salt.\n2. Create a verifier using a slow password-hashing function; store verifier + salt, not plaintext.\n3. At login, retrieve salt/parameters and recompute using entered password.\n4. Compare verifiers and accept/reject; salts reduce hash equality/precomputation.","si":"Registration එකේ නව salt එකක් සාදා verifier එක ගබඩා කරනවා. Login එකේ දැනටමත් ගබඩා කළ salt සහ parameters යොදා verifier එක නැවත ගණනය කර සසඳනවා. Salt එක රහසක් ලෙස තබාගැනීම මෙහි අරමුණ නොවේ.","rubric":[{"point":"Registration: generate unique random salt.","marks":1},{"point":"Create a verifier using a slow password-hashing function; store verifier + salt, not plaintext.","marks":1},{"point":"At login, retrieve salt/parameters and recompute using entered password.","marks":1},{"point":"Compare verifiers and accept/reject; salts reduce hash equality/precomputation.","marks":1}],"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":38,"answerPage":43},{"id":"guide-p2-06","week":10,"part":2,"format":"structured","topic":"Guide structured practice","difficulty":"applied","marks":4,"q":"Describe a challenge–response protocol with a nonce and explain the attack it mitigates.","answer":"1. Server produces a fresh unpredictable challenge/nonce.\n2. Client derives a response from challenge and authentication secret.\n3. Server verifies the correct response for that challenge.\n4. Recorded responses should fail for new challenges, reducing Replay Attacks.","si":"Nonce එක එකවර භාවිත වන අලුත් challenge එකක්. Response එක secret එකටත් එම challenge එකටත් බැඳී තිබිය යුතු නිසා පරණ response එක නැවත එවීම ගැළපෙන්නේ නැහැ. Freshness එකෙන් පමණක් සියලු protocol අවදානම් විසඳෙන්නේ නැහැ.","rubric":[{"point":"Server produces a fresh unpredictable challenge/nonce.","marks":1},{"point":"Client derives a response from challenge and authentication secret.","marks":1},{"point":"Server verifies the correct response for that challenge.","marks":1},{"point":"Recorded responses should fail for new challenges, reducing Replay Attacks.","marks":1}],"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":38,"answerPage":43},{"id":"guide-p2-07","week":11,"part":2,"format":"structured","topic":"Guide structured practice","difficulty":"applied","marks":4,"q":"A service fails at 08:30, starts Alternate Mode at 10:00 and is fully restored at 14:30. Calculate the initial interruption and alternate-mode duration; define SDO.","answer":"1. Initial interruption: 08:30 to 10:00 = 1 h 30 min.\n2. Alternate Mode: 10:00 to 14:30 = 4 h 30 min.\n3. SDO = Service Delivery Objective.\n4. SDO expresses service level intended during alternate operations.","si":"08:30 සිට 10:00 දක්වා මුල් interruption එක පැය 1 මිනිත්තු 30යි. 10:00 සිට 14:30 දක්වා Alternate Mode එක පැය 4 මිනිත්තු 30යි. SDO කියන්නේ එම කාලයේ ලබාදීමට බලාපොරොත්තු වන සේවා මට්ටමයි.","rubric":[{"point":"Initial interruption: 08:30 to 10:00 = 1 h 30 min.","marks":1},{"point":"Alternate Mode: 10:00 to 14:30 = 4 h 30 min.","marks":1},{"point":"SDO = Service Delivery Objective.","marks":1},{"point":"SDO expresses service level intended during alternate operations.","marks":1}],"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":38,"answerPage":44},{"id":"guide-p2-08","week":11,"part":2,"format":"structured","topic":"Guide structured practice","difficulty":"applied","marks":4,"q":"Compare Cold, Hot and Mirrored recovery sites using readiness, speed and cost.","answer":"1. Cold: basic facilities; more setup; slower and less expensive.\n2. Hot: compatible equipment/software available; relatively fast; more expensive.\n3. Mirrored: closely replicated primary site/data; very fast; costly.\n4. Recovery selection depends on criticality and budget; mirroring does not replace backups.","si":"Cold site එක වැඩි සකස් කිරීමක් අවශ්‍ය නිසා සාමාන්‍යයෙන් අඩු වියදම් නමුත් මන්දගාමීයි. Hot සහ Mirrored වඩා සූදානම් නිසා recovery වේගවත් විය හැකි නමුත් වියදම වැඩියි. Site choice එක business අවශ්‍යතාවට සම්බන්ධ කරන්න.","rubric":[{"point":"Cold: basic facilities; more setup; slower and less expensive.","marks":1},{"point":"Hot: compatible equipment/software available; relatively fast; more expensive.","marks":1},{"point":"Mirrored: closely replicated primary site/data; very fast; costly.","marks":1},{"point":"Recovery selection depends on criticality and budget; mirroring does not replace backups.","marks":1}],"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":38,"answerPage":44},{"id":"guide-p2-09","week":11,"part":2,"format":"structured","topic":"Guide structured practice","difficulty":"applied","marks":4,"q":"List the six BCP preparation phases in order and explain why Testing and Maintenance are needed.","answer":"1. Project Initiation → Business/Risk Analysis → Design & Development → Implementation → Testing → Maintenance (credit ordered phases).\n2. Testing validates planned procedures and identifies weaknesses.\n3. Maintenance updates the plan when systems, people and threats change.","si":"Phases හය නිවැරදි අනුපිළිවෙළට ලියා Testing සහ Maintenance සඳහා වෙනම හේතු දෙන්න. Testing එකෙන් සැලැස්ම ක්‍රියාකරනවාද බලන අතර Maintenance එකෙන් නව වෙනස්කම් අනුව එය යාවත්කාලීන කරනවා.","rubric":[{"point":"Project Initiation → Business/Risk Analysis → Design & Development → Implementation → Testing → Maintenance (credit ordered phases).","marks":2},{"point":"Testing validates planned procedures and identifies weaknesses.","marks":1},{"point":"Maintenance updates the plan when systems, people and threats change.","marks":1}],"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":38,"answerPage":44},{"id":"guide-p2-10","week":12,"part":2,"format":"structured","topic":"Guide structured practice","difficulty":"applied","marks":4,"q":"Given ACL rules in order: 1 Deny Internal → 203.0.113.50; 2 Allow Internal → TCP 80; 3 Deny Any. Decide (a) Internal HTTP to 203.0.113.50 and (b) Internal HTTP to 198.51.100.8, justifying first match.","answer":"1. Request (a) matches Rule 1.\n2. It is DENIED even though Rule 2 could permit TCP 80.\n3. Request (b) does not match Rule 1; matches Rule 2.\n4. It is ALLOWED; the first matching rule determines the action.","si":"Rules ඉහළ සිට පහළට පරීක්ෂා කර මුලින්ම match වූ rule එකෙන් තීරණය කරන්න. Block කළ destination එකට Rule 1 නිසා Deny ලැබේ. අනෙක් HTTP request එක Rule 2 නිසා Allow ලැබේ.","rubric":[{"point":"Request (a) matches Rule 1.","marks":1},{"point":"It is DENIED even though Rule 2 could permit TCP 80.","marks":1},{"point":"Request (b) does not match Rule 1; matches Rule 2.","marks":1},{"point":"It is ALLOWED; the first matching rule determines the action.","marks":1}],"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":38,"answerPage":44},{"id":"guide-p2-11","week":12,"part":2,"format":"structured","topic":"Guide structured practice","difficulty":"applied","marks":3,"q":"Define DMZ and briefly distinguish IDS from IPS in a public-web-service deployment.","answer":"1. DMZ isolates public services from sensitive internal network resources.\n2. IDS detects suspicious activity and alerts.\n3. IPS can actively block or interrupt detected malicious traffic.","si":"DMZ එක public services වෙන් කරන network zone එකයි. IDS alerts සඳහාත් IPS blocking වැනි action සඳහාත් යොදාගන්නවා. මෙහි වෙනස් කරුණු තුන සඳහා කෙටි පැහැදිලි points තුනක් ලියන්න.","rubric":[{"point":"DMZ isolates public services from sensitive internal network resources.","marks":1},{"point":"IDS detects suspicious activity and alerts.","marks":1},{"point":"IPS can actively block or interrupt detected malicious traffic.","marks":1}],"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":38,"answerPage":44},{"id":"guide-p3-01","week":9,"part":3,"format":"essay","topic":"University access and identity","difficulty":"challenge","marks":7,"q":"University access & identity (7 marks). A university introduces a single-login portal for students, lecturers and administrators. Students must not edit marks; lecturers can edit assigned-course results; account administrators manage users. Some student passwords have been stolen. Design a suitable access-control and authentication solution.","answer":"1. Choose RBAC and name at least Student, Lecturer and Admin roles.\n2. Allocate least-privilege permissions; Student read own results, Lecturer edit assigned-course results, Admin manage accounts.\n3. Enforce per-resource/per-record authorization after authentication.\n4. Introduce MFA with distinct factors (password + possession/security key).\n5. Use salted slow password verifiers and breached-password response.\n6. Use SSO cautiously with central monitoring and resilience.\n7. Log significant permission changes and suspicious access; separation of duties for sensitive changes.","si":"University එකේ job roles අනුව permissions බෙදීම RBAC එකෙන් කරන්න පුළුවන්. නමුත් login වූ Studentට marks edit කිරීමට අවසර දීම අවශ්‍ය නැහැ; per-record authorizationත් පරීක්ෂා කළ යුතුයි. Stolen passwords නිසා MFA, salted slow verifiers සහ monitoring එකතු කර solution එක scenario එකට සම්බන්ධ කරන්න.","rubric":[{"point":"Choose RBAC and name at least Student, Lecturer and Admin roles.","marks":1},{"point":"Allocate least-privilege permissions; Student read own results, Lecturer edit assigned-course results, Admin manage accounts.","marks":1},{"point":"Enforce per-resource/per-record authorization after authentication.","marks":1},{"point":"Introduce MFA with distinct factors (password + possession/security key).","marks":1},{"point":"Use salted slow password verifiers and breached-password response.","marks":1},{"point":"Use SSO cautiously with central monitoring and resilience.","marks":1},{"point":"Log significant permission changes and suspicious access; separation of duties for sensitive changes.","marks":1}],"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":39,"answerPage":45},{"id":"guide-p3-02","week":11,"part":3,"format":"essay","topic":"Hospital continuity and recovery","difficulty":"challenge","marks":7,"q":"Disaster recovery of an online hospital (7 marks). A hospital data center is damaged by flooding. Emergency clinicians need continued access to essential records. The hospital can fund a well-prepared recovery site but wants to prevent recent data loss. Recommend an integrated DRP and BCP strategy.","answer":"1. Identify Availability and business impact on clinical services.\n2. Provide an Alternate Mode for essential clinical operations, defining SDO.\n3. Select Hot/Mirrored Site based on recovery requirements and funding.\n4. Use appropriate replication/remote journaling to reduce data loss.\n5. Maintain separate protected backups and verify restoration.\n6. Define incident declaration, responsibilities and safety/evacuation procedures.\n7. Conduct periodic recovery testing and plan maintenance.","si":"Cliniciansට essential care දිගටම දීම BC අරමුණයි; බිඳ වැටුණු data center එක නැවත ගොඩනැගීම DR අරමුණයි. Hot හෝ Mirrored site එකක්, සුදුසු replication සහ independent protected backups එකට අවශ්‍යයි. Replication එකෙන් වැරදි හෝ corruptionත් අනෙක් copy එකට යා හැකි නිසා backups අමතක නොකරන්න.","rubric":[{"point":"Identify Availability and business impact on clinical services.","marks":1},{"point":"Provide an Alternate Mode for essential clinical operations, defining SDO.","marks":1},{"point":"Select Hot/Mirrored Site based on recovery requirements and funding.","marks":1},{"point":"Use appropriate replication/remote journaling to reduce data loss.","marks":1},{"point":"Maintain separate protected backups and verify restoration.","marks":1},{"point":"Define incident declaration, responsibilities and safety/evacuation procedures.","marks":1},{"point":"Conduct periodic recovery testing and plan maintenance.","marks":1}],"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":39,"answerPage":45},{"id":"guide-p3-03","week":12,"part":3,"format":"essay","topic":"Network defense and monitoring","difficulty":"challenge","marks":8,"q":"Network breach defense and incident handling (8 marks). A company hosts a public website, an email server and an internal payroll database. An external attacker probes internal ports while suspicious traffic appears on multiple systems. Design a network-security architecture and incident-monitoring strategy.","answer":"1. Place public web and email services in a DMZ.\n2. Keep payroll database in protected internal segment behind restrictive firewall.\n3. Define ACL allow rules for only required services (e.g., TCP 80 web, TCP 25 SMTP in lecture context).\n4. Add Stealth Rule for firewall management and final Cleanup/Default-Deny rule.\n5. Use Stateful Packet Inspection for valid return traffic.\n6. Use IDS/IPS for detection and appropriate blocking.\n7. Use SIEM to correlate logs from firewalls, hosts and applications.\n8. Use anti-spoofing, least privilege, patching and monitoring; a VPN can protect office-to-office links if required.","si":"Public website සහ email services DMZ එකකත් payroll database එක restrictive internal segment එකකත් තබන්න. Firewall rules, stateful inspection, IDS/IPS සහ SIEM එකිනෙකට වෙනස් කාර්ය ඉටු කරයි. එක control එකක් සියලු අවදානම් නවත්වනවා කියා නොලියා layered defense එකේ එක් එක් කොටස අවශ්‍ය හේතුව කියන්න.","rubric":[{"point":"Place public web and email services in a DMZ.","marks":1},{"point":"Keep payroll database in protected internal segment behind restrictive firewall.","marks":1},{"point":"Define ACL allow rules for only required services (e.g., TCP 80 web, TCP 25 SMTP in lecture context).","marks":1},{"point":"Add Stealth Rule for firewall management and final Cleanup/Default-Deny rule.","marks":1},{"point":"Use Stateful Packet Inspection for valid return traffic.","marks":1},{"point":"Use IDS/IPS for detection and appropriate blocking.","marks":1},{"point":"Use SIEM to correlate logs from firewalls, hosts and applications.","marks":1},{"point":"Use anti-spoofing, least privilege, patching and monitoring; a VPN can protect office-to-office links if required.","marks":1}],"source":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","page":39,"answerPage":46}],"glossary":[{"term":"Access Control","en":"Prevent unauthorized use of a resource.","si":"අනවසර user කෙනෙකුට හෝ අනවසර operation එකකට resource භාවිත කිරීම වළක්වයි."},{"term":"Authentication","en":"Verify a claimed identity.","si":"තමන් කවුද කියා කරන claim එකට සාක්ෂි පරීක්ෂා කරයි."},{"term":"Authorization","en":"Determine which actions an identity is permitted to perform.","si":"තහවුරු කළ identity එකට මොන resourcesවල මොන වැඩ කරන්න පුළුවන්ද තීරණය කරයි."},{"term":"DAC","en":"Discretionary sharing based on authorized owners or identities.","si":"Owner හෝ අවසර ඇති පාර්ශ්වය access බෙදාදීම තීරණය කරයි."},{"term":"MAC (Week 9)","en":"Mandatory Access Control using security labels and clearances.","si":"Security labels සහ clearances අනුව මධ්‍යස්ථ නීතියෙන් access තීරණය කරයි."},{"term":"RBAC","en":"Assign permissions to roles and roles to users.","si":"Job role එකට permissions දී එම role එක userට ලබාදෙයි."},{"term":"ACL","en":"An object-associated list of subjects and access rights.","si":"එක් resource එකකට කාට මොන rights තිබේද ලැයිස්තුගත කරයි."},{"term":"Capability","en":"An unforgeable resource-authority token or reference.","si":"Holderට නිශ්චිත resource බලයක් දෙන forge කළ නොහැකි reference එකකි."},{"term":"Least Privilege","en":"Grant only the minimum permissions needed.","si":"වැඩේ කිරීමට අවශ්‍ය අවම අවසර පමණක් දෙයි."},{"term":"Separation of Duty","en":"Divide critical tasks among different people.","si":"Sensitive workflow පියවර වෙනස් අය අතර වෙන් කරයි."},{"term":"Dual Control","en":"Require multiple authorized people for a critical action.","si":"එකම sensitive ක්‍රියාවට අවසර ඇති පුද්ගලයන් කිහිපදෙනෙකු එක්ව අවශ්‍ය කරයි."},{"term":"MFA","en":"Authentication using independent factor categories.","si":"Know, Have, Are හෝ Do වැනි වෙනස් categoriesවල සාක්ෂි භාවිත කරයි."},{"term":"SSO","en":"One central authentication arrangement for associated services.","si":"එක් login සැකසුමකින් සම්බන්ධ සේවා කිහිපයකට පිවිසෙයි."},{"term":"Salt","en":"A unique random input used with password hashing.","si":"එකම passwordටත් වෙනස් verifier ලැබීමට hashing input එක වෙනස් කරයි."},{"term":"Challenge–Response","en":"Fresh challenge plus a secret-dependent response.","si":"අලුත් nonce එකකට secret එකට බැඳුණු අලුත් response එකක් ඉල්ලයි."},{"term":"DRP","en":"Restore disrupted systems, data and infrastructure.","si":"බිඳ වැටුණු පද්ධති, දත්ත සහ infrastructure නැවත යථා තත්ත්වයට පත් කරයි."},{"term":"BCP","en":"Maintain essential operations during disruption.","si":"බාධාව තිබියදීත් අත්‍යවශ්‍ය ව්‍යාපාරික වැඩ කරගෙන යයි."},{"term":"SDO","en":"The target service level in Alternate Mode.","si":"තාවකාලික වැඩ කරන ආකාරයේ ලබාදීමට බලාපොරොත්තු වන සේවා මට්ටමයි."},{"term":"Cold / Hot / Mirrored","en":"Basic facility / prepared infrastructure / closely replicated site.","si":"සූදානම්භාවය සහ වියදම අනුව recovery වේගය වෙනස් වන site විකල්ප වේ."},{"term":"Stealth / Cleanup","en":"Protect the firewall itself / deny otherwise unmatched traffic.","si":"Stealth එක firewall එකම ආරක්ෂා කරයි; Cleanup එක ඉතිරි traffic deny කරයි."},{"term":"Stateful Firewall","en":"Track packets against authorized session state.","si":"Packet එක allowed connection එකක කොටසක්ද කියා state සමඟ සසඳයි."},{"term":"DMZ","en":"Separate public-facing services from sensitive internal resources.","si":"Public servers සහ confidential internal systems වෙනස් network zonesවල වෙන් කරයි."},{"term":"IDS / IPS","en":"Detect and alert / detect and take preventive action.","si":"IDS alert දෙයි; IPS blocking වැනි ක්‍රියාත්මක වැළැක්වීමක් ගත හැකියි."},{"term":"SIEM","en":"Collect and correlate security events from multiple sources.","si":"විවිධ systemsවල logs එකතු කර සම්බන්ධ කර බලයි."},{"term":"UTM","en":"Combine several gateway security controls in one system.","si":"Firewall සහ filtering වැනි security functions කිහිපයක් එකට ලබාදෙයි."},{"term":"VPN","en":"A protected logical tunnel across a shared or untrusted network.","si":"Public network එකක් හරහා endpoints අතර protected tunnel එකක් ලබාදෙයි."}],"quickChecks":[{"q":"A manager grants Read only. May Write be assumed?","a":"No. Only explicitly granted rights may be exercised.","si":"R තිබුණා කියා W ලැබෙන්නේ නැහැ. Permission එක පැහැදිලිව පරීක්ෂා කරන්න."},{"q":"Is a PIN plus a password definitely two-factor authentication?","a":"No. Both are knowledge factors.","si":"එකම factor category එකේ රහස් දෙකක් දීම MFA නොවේ."},{"q":"Failure is at 09:00; alternate service begins at 10:15. What is the interruption duration?","a":"1 hour 15 minutes.","si":"Failure වෙලාවේ සිට essential service නැවත ලැබෙන වෙලාව දක්වා ගණනය කරන්න."},{"q":"A packet first matches Deny and later matches Allow. What happens?","a":"Deny, under the guide’s first-match ACL model.","si":"මුලින් match වූ rule එක ක්‍රියාත්මක කර නවතී; පසුව ඇති allow එක බලන්නේ නැහැ."},{"q":"Normal traffic triggers an IDS alarm. TP, FP, TN or FN?","a":"False Positive (FP).","si":"සැබෑ තත්ත්වය normal නමුත් alarm positive නිසා False Positive වේ."}],"traps":[{"trigger":"A logged-in user cannot edit a record.","answer":"Authorization or RBAC, not failed authentication.","si":"Login සාර්ථක වුණත් edit permission වෙනම අවශ්‍යයි."},{"trigger":"The same password is used with different salts.","answer":"Distinct stored verifiers; the salt does not add password entropy.","si":"Salt එකෙන් hashing input වෙනස් කරයි; user password එකේ අනුමාන කළ නොහැකි බව ස්වයංක්‍රීයව වැඩි කරන්නේ නැහැ."},{"trigger":"Yesterday’s valid response is resent.","answer":"Replay attack; require a fresh challenge and a correctly bound response.","si":"පරණ response එක නව nonce එකට ගැළපෙන්නේ නැති විය යුතුයි."},{"trigger":"Two people approve the same sensitive action.","answer":"Dual Control; distinguish this from different workflow steps.","si":"වෙනස් පියවර වෙන් කිරීම SoD වන අතර එකම ක්‍රියාවට එක්ව සහභාගී වීම Dual Control වේ."},{"trigger":"A catch-all deny appears before a required allow.","answer":"A rule-order error can shadow the later allow.","si":"First-match ක්‍රමයේ කලින් deny එකෙන් නවතින නිසා පසු allow rule එකට ළඟා නොවෙයි."},{"trigger":"A public website is placed beside an internal database.","answer":"Use a DMZ and restrictive inner access controls.","si":"Public service එක compromise වුණත් internal database එකට unrestricted access නොලැබෙන ලෙස zones වෙන් කරන්න."},{"trigger":"Primary database restoration versus temporary backup-site service.","answer":"DR restores; BC continues essential operations.","si":"මුල් පද්ධතිය නැවත හදන වැඩ සහ බාධාව අතරතුර සේවාව පවත්වාගන්නා වැඩ වෙනම හඳුනාගන්න."}],"routine":["එක් chapter එකක් කියවා එහි diagramsවල arrows සහ decisions ඔබම විස්තර කරන්න.","පොත වසා checkpoint ප්‍රශ්නවලට මතකයෙන් English පිළිතුරු කියන්න හෝ ලියන්න.","Question clinic එකේ scenarios සඳහා answer බැලීමට පෙර ඔබේ reasoning එක ලියන්න.","Weeks 9–12 guide mock එක notes නැතිව attempt කර සියලු questionsවලට පිළිතුරු දෙන්න.","Model answers සහ rubrics යොදා self-mark කර වැරදුණු topics නැවත revise කරන්න."],"attributionNote":"Clinic cases are adapted practice from the supplied guide. Specific 2024 labels in that guide are not independently verified here.","scope":"Weeks 9–12 topic-focused practice; not an official prediction and not a replacement for Weeks 1–8 revision.","source":{"original":"IT3070_Weeks_9_to_12_Sinhala_Self_Study_Guide.pdf","label":"Weeks 9–12 Sinhala Self-Study Guide","pages":49,"url":"materials/weeks9-12-self-study-guide.pdf","note":"Supplied handbook · illustrated web lessons and completed worked answers"},"topicCount":22,"diagramCount":21};
